{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":143678},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":22717557}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"code","source":"# This Python 3 environment comes with many helpful analytics libraries installed\n# It is defined by the kaggle/python Docker image: https://github.com/kaggle/docker-python\n# For example, here's several helpful packages to load\n\nimport numpy as np # linear algebra\nimport pandas as pd # data processing, CSV file I/O (e.g. pd.read_csv)\n\n# Input data files are available in the read-only \"../input/\" directory\n# For example, running this (by clicking run or pressing Shift+Enter) will list all files under the input directory\n\nimport os\nfor dirname, _, filenames in os.walk('/kaggle/input'):\n    for filename in filenames:\n        print(os.path.join(dirname, filename))\n\n# You can write up to 20GB to the current directory (/kaggle/working/) that gets preserved as output when you create a version using \"Save & Run All\" \n# You can also write temporary files to /kaggle/temp/, but they won't be saved outside of the current session\n\n# Use the kagglehub client library to attach Kaggle resources like competitions, datasets, and models to your session\n# Learn more about kagglehub: https://github.com/Kaggle/kagglehub/blob/main/README.md\n\nimport kagglehub\n# kagglehub.dataset_download('<owner>/<dataset-slug>')","metadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","trusted":true,"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Pipeline vision\n\n1. Stage 1 — Ground-truth validation\n   \n   COCO rasterization, RLE round trips, mask-area agreement, image integrity.\n\n2. Stage 2 — Dataset and annotator analysis\n   \n   Audit all image dimensions, unmatched JPEGs, image quality, annotation disagreement, and foreground coverage.\n3. Stage 3 — Leakage-free dataset construction\n   \n   Finalize five physical-photo folds, annotation sampling, tile extraction and augmentation.\n4. Stage 4 — Classical computer-vision baseline\n   \n   Intensity normalization, adaptive thresholding, morphological reconstruction and connected components. Establish a non-neural reference.\n5. Stage 5 — Deep-learning baseline\n   \n   Native-resolution tiled U-Net with BCE + Dice. Train, validate and save checkpoints.\n6. Stage 6 — Scientific contributions and ablations\n   \n   Tversky loss, clDice, auxiliary spine supervision and spine-seeded instance splitting.\n7. Stage 7 — Instance-level evaluation\n   \n   Official PQ, Dice, IoU, fragmentation, merging, annotator ceiling and failure analysis.\n8. Stage 8 — Inference and submission\n   \n   Sliding-window inference, overlap blending, test-time augmentation, instance extraction and RLE CSV generation.\n9. Stage 9 — Reproducibility and reporting\n   \n   Public repository, pinned dependencies, saved weights, complete inference notebook and technical report.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Section I - PATH CONFIG & COCO JSON INSPECTION","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"DATASET_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026\")\n\nTRAIN_IMG_DIR = Path (\"/kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026/train/train_images\")\nTRAIN_JSON_PATH = Path (\"/kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026/train/MAGFiLO_1.0_Annotations_kaggle2026_train.json\")\n\nTEST_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026/test/test_images\")\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Load and Parse COCO JSON file","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Parsing COCO JSON file ...\")\nwith open (TRAIN_JSON_PATH,'r') as f:\n        coco_data = json.load(f)\n\n# Top-level keys in json format:\nprint(f\"Top-level JSON Keys: {list(coco_data.keys())}\")\n\n# Summary Statistics of Data \nimages_list = coco_data['images']\nannotations_list = coco_data[\"annotations\"]\ncategories_list = coco_data[\"categories\"]\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Dataset Overview ---\")\nprint(f\"Total Annotation Entries (image['id']): {len(images_list)}\")\nprint(f\"Total Filament Instances (annotations):  {len(annotations_list)}\")\nprint(f\"Categories Found:                       {categories_list}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Dataset integrity audit\n\nAudit all 707 physical photographs, not just the sample.\n\nBefore training, we must establish that our input images are usable and that the metadata correctly describes them.\n\nWe will investigate:\n1. Are all referenced JPEGs actually present?\n2. Are images readable and exactly 2048 × 2048?\n3. Are they genuinely grayscale, as specified by the competition?\n4. Are there blank, corrupted or unusually saturated images?\n5. Are there unexpected files or filename-format problems?\n6. Does every annotation point to a valid COCO image entry?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# STAGE 2A: PHYSICAL IMAGE INTEGRITY AUDIT\n# ============================================================\n\nimport cv2\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Map annotation batches to physical photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphysical_file_to_image_ids = defaultdict(list)\n\nfor img_info in images_list:\n    physical_file_to_image_ids[img_info[\"file_name\"]].append(\n        img_info[\"id\"]\n    )\n\nid_to_file = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img[\"file_name\"]\n    for img in images_list\n}\n\nreferenced_files = set(physical_file_to_image_ids.keys())\n\n# Duplicate image IDs in COCO JSON\nimage_id_counts = Counter(img[\"id\"] for img in images_list)\n\nduplicate_image_ids = [\n    image_id for image_id, count in image_id_counts.items()\n    if count > 1\n]\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Compare JSON-referenced photographs with disk contents\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nif not TRAIN_IMG_DIR.is_dir():\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\n        f\"Training image directory missing: {TRAIN_IMG_DIR}\"\n    )\n\ndisk_files = {\n    p.name for p in TRAIN_IMG_DIR.iterdir()\n    if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() in {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\"}\n}\n\nmissing_files = sorted(referenced_files - disk_files)\nextra_files = sorted(disk_files - referenced_files)\n\n# Annotation counts by batch ID\nannotation_counts = Counter(\n    ann[\"image_id\"] for ann in annotations_list\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Audit every unique physical photograph\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nexpected_height = 2048\nexpected_width = 2048\n\nfilename_pattern = re.compile(\n    r\"^(?P<timestamp>\\d{14})(?P<site>[A-Za-z]{2})\\.jpe?g$\",\n    re.IGNORECASE\n)\n\naudit_rows = []\n\nfor index, file_name in enumerate(sorted(referenced_files), start=1):\n\n    path = TRAIN_IMG_DIR / file_name\n\n    row = {\n        \"file_name\": file_name,\n        \"n_batches\": len(physical_file_to_image_ids[file_name]),\n        \"n_annotations\": sum(\n            annotation_counts[batch_id]\n            for batch_id in physical_file_to_image_ids[file_name]\n        ),\n        \"file_exists\": path.is_file(),\n        \"decoded\": False,\n        \"shape_ok\": False,\n        \"dtype_ok\": False,\n        \"grayscale_ok\": False,\n        \"dynamic_range_ok\": False,\n        \"filename_format_ok\": False,\n        \"timestamp_valid\": False,\n        \"site_code\": None,\n        \"height\": None,\n        \"width\": None,\n        \"dtype\": None,\n        \"min_intensity\": None,\n        \"max_intensity\": None,\n        \"mean_intensity\": None,\n        \"std_intensity\": None,\n        \"p01\": None,\n        \"p50\": None,\n        \"p99\": None,\n        \"fraction_zero\": None,\n        \"fraction_255\": None,\n        \"unique_intensity_levels\": None\n    }\n\n    # Filename and timestamp validation\n    match = filename_pattern.fullmatch(file_name)\n\n    if match:\n        row[\"filename_format_ok\"] = True\n        row[\"site_code\"] = match.group(\"site\")\n\n        try:\n            datetime.strptime(\n                match.group(\"timestamp\"),\n                \"%Y%m%d%H%M%S\"\n            )\n            row[\"timestamp_valid\"] = True\n        except ValueError:\n            pass\n\n    if path.is_file():\n\n        # Read original encoding without forcing grayscale\n        img = cv2.imread(\n            str(path),\n            cv2.IMREAD_UNCHANGED\n        )\n\n        if img is not None:\n\n            row[\"decoded\"] = True\n\n            height, width = img.shape[:2]\n\n            row[\"height\"] = height\n            row[\"width\"] = width\n\n            row[\"shape_ok\"] = (\n                height == expected_height\n                and width == expected_width\n            )\n\n            row[\"dtype\"] = str(img.dtype)\n            row[\"dtype_ok\"] = img.dtype == np.uint8\n\n            # Determine whether the stored image is grayscale\n            if img.ndim == 2:\n\n                gray = img\n                row[\"grayscale_ok\"] = True\n\n            elif img.ndim == 3 and img.shape[2] == 3:\n\n                row[\"grayscale_ok\"] = (\n                    np.array_equal(img[:, :, 0], img[:, :, 1])\n                    and np.array_equal(img[:, :, 1], img[:, :, 2])\n                )\n\n                gray = cv2.cvtColor(\n                    img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2GRAY\n                )\n\n            elif img.ndim == 3 and img.shape[2] == 4:\n\n                row[\"grayscale_ok\"] = (\n                    np.array_equal(img[:, :, 0], img[:, :, 1])\n                    and np.array_equal(img[:, :, 1], img[:, :, 2])\n                )\n\n                gray = cv2.cvtColor(\n                    img, cv2.COLOR_BGRA2GRAY\n                )\n\n            else:\n                gray = None\n\n            if gray is not None:\n\n                pixels = gray.reshape(-1)\n\n                min_val = int(pixels.min())\n                max_val = int(pixels.max())\n\n                row[\"min_intensity\"] = min_val\n                row[\"max_intensity\"] = max_val\n                row[\"mean_intensity\"] = float(pixels.mean())\n                row[\"std_intensity\"] = float(pixels.std())\n\n                p01, p50, p99 = np.percentile(\n                    pixels, [1, 50, 99]\n                )\n\n                row[\"p01\"] = float(p01)\n                row[\"p50\"] = float(p50)\n                row[\"p99\"] = float(p99)\n\n                row[\"fraction_zero\"] = float(\n                    np.mean(pixels == 0)\n                )\n\n                row[\"fraction_255\"] = float(\n                    np.mean(pixels == 255)\n                )\n\n                row[\"unique_intensity_levels\"] = int(\n                    np.unique(pixels).size\n                )\n\n                row[\"dynamic_range_ok\"] = max_val > min_val\n\n    audit_rows.append(row)\n\n    if index % 100 == 0:\n        print(f\"Audited {index}/{len(referenced_files)} photographs\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Generate audit DataFrame\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphoto_audit_df = pd.DataFrame(audit_rows)\n\nrequired_checks = [\n    \"file_exists\",\n    \"decoded\",\n    \"shape_ok\",\n    \"dtype_ok\",\n    \"grayscale_ok\",\n    \"dynamic_range_ok\",\n    \"filename_format_ok\",\n    \"timestamp_valid\"\n]\n\nphoto_audit_df[\"valid_for_pipeline\"] = (\n    photo_audit_df[required_checks].all(axis=1)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Cross-reference JSON annotations against images\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nknown_image_ids = set(id_to_file.keys())\n\nunknown_annotation_image_ids = sorted(\n    set(ann[\"image_id\"] for ann in annotations_list)\n    - known_image_ids\n)\n\nannotation_ids = [\n    ann[\"id\"] for ann in annotations_list\n]\n\nduplicate_annotation_ids = [\n    ann_id for ann_id, count in Counter(annotation_ids).items()\n    if count > 1\n]\n\nknown_category_ids = {\n    category[\"id\"] for category in categories_list\n}\n\nunknown_category_ids = sorted(\n    set(ann[\"category_id\"] for ann in annotations_list)\n    - known_category_ids\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Print results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"PHYSICAL IMAGE INTEGRITY AUDIT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", len(images_list))\nprint(\"Unique physical photographs:\", len(referenced_files))\nprint(\"JPEG files on disk:\", len(disk_files))\nprint(\"Images referenced but missing:\", len(missing_files))\nprint(\"Unreferenced JPEGs on disk:\", len(extra_files))\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Image Quality Checks ---\")\n\nfor check in required_checks:\n    print(\n        f\"{check:25s}: \"\n        f\"{int(photo_audit_df[check].sum())}/\"\n        f\"{len(photo_audit_df)}\"\n    )\n\nprint(\n    \"\\nImages passing all checks:\",\n    int(photo_audit_df[\"valid_for_pipeline\"].sum()),\n    \"/\",\n    len(photo_audit_df)\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- COCO Referential Integrity ---\")\n\nprint(\"Duplicate image IDs:\", len(duplicate_image_ids))\nprint(\"Unknown image references:\", len(unknown_annotation_image_ids))\nprint(\"Duplicate annotation IDs:\", len(duplicate_annotation_ids))\nprint(\"Unknown category references:\", len(unknown_category_ids))\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7. Show anomalous photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfailed_images = photo_audit_df[\n    ~photo_audit_df[\"valid_for_pipeline\"]\n]\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Photographs Requiring Inspection ---\")\n\nif failed_images.empty:\n    print(\"All referenced images passed the structural checks.\")\nelse:\n    display(\n        failed_images[\n            [\n                \"file_name\",\n                \"n_batches\",\n                \"height\",\n                \"width\",\n                \"dtype\",\n                \"grayscale_ok\",\n                \"filename_format_ok\",\n                \"timestamp_valid\"\n            ]\n        ]\n    )\n\n# Intensity statistics: descriptive, not automatic rejection criteria\nprint(\"\\n--- Intensity Distribution Summary ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    photo_audit_df[\n        [\n            \"mean_intensity\",\n            \"std_intensity\",\n            \"p01\",\n            \"p50\",\n            \"p99\",\n            \"fraction_zero\",\n            \"fraction_255\"\n        ]\n    ].describe().round(4)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Save audit results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)\n\nphoto_audit_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"photo_integrity_audit.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"\\nAudit saved:\",\n    WORK_DIR / \"photo_integrity_audit.csv\"\n)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"photo_audit_df.sample(10)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Sample Inspection of Metadata ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"sample_img = images_list[0]\nsample_ann = annotations_list[0]\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Sample Image Entry ---\")\nprint(json.dumps(sample_img, indent=2))\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Sample Annotation Entry ---\")\n# Shorten the long list arrays just for pretty printing\nsample_ann_print = sample_ann.copy()\nsample_ann_print[\"segmentation\"] = f\"[{len(sample_ann['segmentation'][0])} coordinate values]\"\nsample_ann_print[\"spine\"] = f\"[{len(sample_ann['spine'])} coordinate values]\"\nprint(json.dumps(sample_ann_print, indent=2))","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Mask Rasterization - Visual Overlay gen.\n\nThe given annotations coco json contains the polygon coordinates identifying the objects(filaments) in each images - This is done for efficient storage of entities from each image over storing the entire mask in gigabytes.\n\nBut Neural Networks understands tensors and not 2d cooridnates - thus we need to rasterize them into masks\n\n**Rasterization** is the process of converting a vector-based or mathematical representation of an image, shape, or object into a grid of pixels (a raster image) that can be displayed on a screen or stored as an image.\n\nFor example:\n```\n   Vector Data\t       Rasterized Output\n\nRoad line\t        Pixels representing the road\nBuilding polygon        Filled pixel region\nLandslide boundary\tBinary mask image\nRiver shapefile\t        Raster layer\n```","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Mapping image files to their respective annotations\n\nThis answers:\n\n\"Which annotations belong to each COCO image ID?\"","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"image_id_to_anns = defaultdict(list)\nfor ann in coco_data[\"annotations\"]:\n    image_id_to_anns[ann[\"image_id\"]].append(ann)\n\nprint(f\"Mapped annotations for {len(image_id_to_anns)} unique image IDs.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Polygon & Spine Rasterization ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from pycocotools import mask as mask_utils\nimport numpy as np\nimport cv2\n\n\ndef polygon_to_mask(segmentation, height, width):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rasterize COCO polygon segmentation using pycocotools.\n    Returns a binary uint8 mask.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(segmentation, list) or not segmentation:\n        raise ValueError(\"Annotation has no polygon segmentation.\")\n\n    polygons = []\n\n    for polygon in segmentation:\n        coords = np.asarray(polygon, dtype=np.float64)\n\n        if coords.ndim != 1 or coords.size < 6 or coords.size % 2 != 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid polygon coordinates.\")\n\n        if not np.isfinite(coords).all():\n            raise ValueError(\"Non-finite polygon coordinates.\")\n\n        polygons.append(coords.tolist())\n\n    rles = mask_utils.frPyObjects(\n        polygons, int(height), int(width)\n    )\n\n    rle = mask_utils.merge(rles) if isinstance(rles, list) else rles\n    mask = mask_utils.decode(rle)\n\n    if mask.ndim == 3:\n        mask = np.any(mask > 0, axis=2)\n\n    return (mask > 0).astype(np.uint8)\n\n\ndef create_filament_mask(\n    annotations,\n    height=2048,\n    width=2048,\n    spine_thickness=3\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns:\n        combined_mask: union of all filament instances\n        spine_mask: combined spine-band target\n        instance_masks: independent binary masks per filament\n    \"\"\"\n\n    height, width = int(height), int(width)\n\n    if height <= 0 or width <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid image dimensions.\")\n\n    combined_mask = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=np.uint8)\n    spine_mask = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=np.uint8)\n\n    instance_masks = []\n\n    for ann in annotations:\n\n        # 1. Filament segmentation: COCO rasterization\n        inst_mask = polygon_to_mask(\n            ann.get(\"segmentation\", []),\n            height,\n            width\n        )\n\n        if not inst_mask.any():\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Empty segmentation: {ann.get('id')}\"\n            )\n\n        instance_masks.append(inst_mask)\n        combined_mask |= inst_mask\n\n        # 2. Auxiliary spine rasterization\n        spine_coords = ann.get(\"spine\", [])\n\n        if spine_coords:\n            spine_coords = np.asarray(\n                spine_coords, dtype=np.float64\n            )\n\n            if (\n                spine_coords.ndim != 1\n                or spine_coords.size < 4\n                or spine_coords.size % 2 != 0\n                or not np.isfinite(spine_coords).all()\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"Malformed spine: {ann.get('id')}\"\n                )\n\n            spine_points = np.rint(\n                spine_coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n            ).astype(np.int32).reshape(-1, 1, 2)\n\n            cv2.polylines(\n                spine_mask,\n                [spine_points],\n                isClosed=False,\n                color=1,\n                thickness=spine_thickness,\n                lineType=cv2.LINE_8\n            )\n\n    return combined_mask, spine_mask, instance_masks\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Sample test of rasterizer on first image","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### What we are testing:\n1. Every annotation produces a non-empty mask.\n2. The mask dimensions are correct.\n3. The rasterized pixel area agrees with the stored COCO area.\n4. We quantify how much the previous OpenCV implementation differs from the COCO reference.\nWe will use the COCO implementation as our authoritative rasterizer, regardless of whether the previous method happens to agree on the sampled annotations.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Validate COCO polygon rasterization\n\nsample_img_info = images_list[0]\nsample_img_id = sample_img_info[\"id\"]\nsample_file_name = sample_img_info[\"file_name\"]\n\nsample_anns = image_id_to_anns[sample_img_id]\n\nheight = int(sample_img_info[\"height\"])\nwidth = int(sample_img_info[\"width\"])\n\ncombined_mask, spine_mask, inst_masks = create_filament_mask(\n    sample_anns,\n    height=height,\n    width=width,\n    spine_thickness=3\n)\n\nassert len(inst_masks) == len(sample_anns)\nassert combined_mask.shape == (height, width)\nassert spine_mask.shape == (height, width)\n\nassert set(np.unique(combined_mask)).issubset({0, 1})\nassert set(np.unique(spine_mask)).issubset({0, 1})\n\ncoverage_pct = 100.0 * combined_mask.sum() / combined_mask.size\n\n\n# Previous OpenCV rasterization, retained only for comparison\ndef cv2_truncated_polygon_mask(segmentation, height, width):\n\n    out = np.zeros((height, width), dtype=np.uint8)\n\n    pts = np.asarray(\n        segmentation[0], dtype=np.float32\n    ).reshape(-1, 2).astype(np.int32)\n\n    cv2.fillPoly(out, [pts], 1)\n\n    return out\n\n\n# Compare 100 randomly selected annotations\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n\nn_compare = min(100, len(annotations_list))\n\nsample_indices = rng.choice(\n    len(annotations_list),\n    size=n_compare,\n    replace=False\n)\n\ncomparison_ious = []\ncomparison_xor_pixels = []\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    im[\"id\"]: im for im in images_list\n}\n\nfor idx in sample_indices:\n\n    ann = annotations_list[int(idx)]\n\n    info = image_info_by_id[ann[\"image_id\"]]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    coco_mask = polygon_to_mask(\n        ann[\"segmentation\"], h, w\n    )\n\n    cv_mask = cv2_truncated_polygon_mask(\n        ann[\"segmentation\"], h, w\n    )\n\n    intersection = np.logical_and(\n        coco_mask, cv_mask\n    ).sum()\n\n    union = np.logical_or(\n        coco_mask, cv_mask\n    ).sum()\n\n    iou = intersection / union if union else 1.0\n\n    comparison_ious.append(float(iou))\n\n    comparison_xor_pixels.append(\n        int(np.logical_xor(coco_mask, cv_mask).sum())\n    )\n\n\n# Compare original area field with COCO-rasterized pixel area\narea_abs_errors = [\n    abs(float(ann[\"area\"]) - float(mask.sum()))\n    for ann, mask in zip(sample_anns, inst_masks)\n]\n\n\nprint(\"Sample batch:\", sample_img_id)\nprint(\"Physical image:\", sample_file_name)\nprint(\"Number of instances:\", len(inst_masks))\n\nprint(\"Combined foreground pixels:\", int(combined_mask.sum()))\nprint(f\"Foreground coverage: {coverage_pct:.4f}%\")\n\nprint(\n    \"Maximum stored-area discrepancy:\",\n    f\"{max(area_abs_errors):.3f} px²\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    f\"OpenCV vs COCO IoU ({n_compare} annotations):\",\n    f\"Mean={np.mean(comparison_ious):.6f}\",\n    f\"Median={np.median(comparison_ious):.6f}\",\n    f\"Minimum={np.min(comparison_ious):.6f}\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"OpenCV vs COCO XOR pixels:\",\n    f\"Median={np.median(comparison_xor_pixels):.0f}\",\n    f\"Maximum={max(comparison_xor_pixels)}\"\n)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual Overlay","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Load the actual training image\n\nimg_path = TRAIN_IMG_DIR / sample_file_name\n\nif not img_path.is_file():\n    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Missing image: {img_path}\")\n\nraw_img = cv2.imread(\n    str(img_path),\n    cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n)\n\nif raw_img is None:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot decode image: {img_path}\")\n\nexpected_shape = (\n    int(sample_img_info[\"height\"]),\n    int(sample_img_info[\"width\"])\n)\n\nif raw_img.shape != expected_shape:\n    raise ValueError(\n        f\"Unexpected shape: {raw_img.shape}, \"\n        f\"expected {expected_shape}\"\n    )\n\nif raw_img.dtype != np.uint8:\n    raise TypeError(\"Expected uint8 grayscale image.\")\n\nif raw_img.max() == raw_img.min():\n    raise ValueError(\"Image has no intensity variation.\")\n\n\n# Alpha-blended filament overlay\nbase_rgb = cv2.cvtColor(\n    raw_img,\n    cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB\n)\n\nbody_overlay = base_rgb.copy()\n\nbody_overlay[combined_mask > 0] = (255, 50, 50)\n\noverlay_img = cv2.addWeighted(\n    base_rgb,\n    0.65,\n    body_overlay,\n    0.35,\n    0\n)\n\noverlay_img[spine_mask > 0] = (0, 255, 255)\n\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 6))\n\naxes[0].imshow(raw_img, cmap=\"gray\")\naxes[0].set_title(\n    f\"Original H-alpha observation\\n{sample_file_name}\"\n)\naxes[0].axis(\"off\")\n\naxes[1].imshow(combined_mask, cmap=\"gray\", vmin=0, vmax=1)\naxes[1].set_title(\n    f\"COCO semantic mask\\n{len(inst_masks)} instances\"\n)\naxes[1].axis(\"off\")\n\naxes[2].imshow(overlay_img)\naxes[2].set_title(\n    \"Red: Filament | Cyan: Spine\"\n)\naxes[2].axis(\"off\")\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Spine Supervision Validation\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# FINAL ARCHITECTURE PREPARATION:\n# SPINE TARGET QUALITY AUDIT\n# ============================================================\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport cv2\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSPINE_THICKNESS = 3\n\nbatch_spine_records = []\nannotation_spine_records = []\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Create semantic and spine targets without retaining\n#    separate instance masks in memory.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef build_semantic_spine_targets(\n    annotations,\n    height,\n    width,\n    spine_thickness=3\n):\n\n    semantic_mask = np.zeros(\n        (height, width), dtype=np.uint8\n    )\n\n    spine_mask = np.zeros(\n        (height, width), dtype=np.uint8\n    )\n\n    for ann in annotations:\n\n        semantic_mask |= polygon_to_mask(\n            ann[\"segmentation\"],\n            height,\n            width\n        )\n\n        raw_spine = ann.get(\"spine\", [])\n\n        if raw_spine is None or len(raw_spine) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        coords = np.asarray(\n            raw_spine,\n            dtype=np.float64\n        )\n\n        if (\n            coords.ndim != 1\n            or coords.size < 4\n            or coords.size % 2 != 0\n            or not np.isfinite(coords).all()\n        ):\n            continue\n\n        points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n        points_int = np.rint(\n            points\n        ).astype(np.int32).reshape(-1, 1, 2)\n\n        cv2.polylines(\n            spine_mask,\n            [points_int],\n            isClosed=False,\n            color=1,\n            thickness=spine_thickness,\n            lineType=cv2.LINE_8\n        )\n\n    return semantic_mask, spine_mask\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Validate each annotation's spine coordinates\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ninvalid_spines = []\nmissing_spines = 0\nout_of_bounds_spines = 0\nvalid_spines = 0\n\nfor ann in annotations_list:\n\n    info = image_info_by_id.get(\n        ann[\"image_id\"]\n    )\n\n    if info is None:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Missing image metadata: {ann['image_id']}\"\n        )\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    raw_spine = ann.get(\"spine\", [])\n\n    if raw_spine is None or len(raw_spine) == 0:\n\n        missing_spines += 1\n\n        annotation_spine_records.append({\n            \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n            \"valid_spine\": False,\n            \"missing\": True\n        })\n\n        continue\n\n    coords = np.asarray(\n        raw_spine,\n        dtype=np.float64\n    )\n\n    valid_format = (\n        coords.ndim == 1\n        and coords.size >= 4\n        and coords.size % 2 == 0\n        and np.isfinite(coords).all()\n    )\n\n    if not valid_format:\n\n        invalid_spines.append(ann[\"id\"])\n\n        annotation_spine_records.append({\n            \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n            \"valid_spine\": False,\n            \"missing\": False\n        })\n\n        continue\n\n    points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    out_of_bounds = np.any(\n        (points[:, 0] < 0)\n        | (points[:, 0] >= w)\n        | (points[:, 1] < 0)\n        | (points[:, 1] >= h)\n    )\n\n    if out_of_bounds:\n        out_of_bounds_spines += 1\n\n    spine_length = np.linalg.norm(\n        np.diff(points, axis=0),\n        axis=1\n    ).sum()\n\n    if spine_length <= 0:\n\n        invalid_spines.append(ann[\"id\"])\n\n        annotation_spine_records.append({\n            \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n            \"valid_spine\": False,\n            \"missing\": False\n        })\n\n        continue\n\n    valid_spines += 1\n\n    annotation_spine_records.append({\n\n        \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n\n        \"valid_spine\": True,\n\n        \"missing\": False,\n\n        \"spine_length_px\": float(spine_length),\n\n        \"spine_points\": len(points),\n\n        \"out_of_bounds\": bool(out_of_bounds)\n\n    })\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Measure spatial overlap between spine bands and masks\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfor idx, info in enumerate(images_list):\n\n    batch_id = info[\"id\"]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    annotations = image_id_to_anns.get(\n        batch_id, []\n    )\n\n    foreground, spine = build_semantic_spine_targets(\n        annotations,\n        h,\n        w,\n        SPINE_THICKNESS\n    )\n\n    foreground_pixels = int(foreground.sum())\n    spine_pixels = int(spine.sum())\n\n    overlap_pixels = int(\n        np.logical_and(\n            foreground > 0,\n            spine > 0\n        ).sum()\n    )\n\n    outside_pixels = spine_pixels - overlap_pixels\n\n    batch_spine_records.append({\n\n        \"image_id\": batch_id,\n\n        \"file_name\": info[\"file_name\"],\n\n        \"n_annotations\": len(annotations),\n\n        \"foreground_pixels\": foreground_pixels,\n\n        \"spine_pixels\": spine_pixels,\n\n        \"spine_inside_foreground\": overlap_pixels,\n\n        \"spine_outside_foreground\": outside_pixels,\n\n        \"spine_inside_fraction\": (\n            overlap_pixels / spine_pixels\n            if spine_pixels > 0 else np.nan\n        ),\n\n        \"spine_band_to_foreground_pct\": (\n            100 * spine_pixels / foreground_pixels\n            if foreground_pixels > 0 else np.nan\n        )\n\n    })\n\n    del foreground, spine\n\n    if (idx + 1) % 200 == 0:\n        print(\n            f\"Audited {idx+1}/{len(images_list)} batches\"\n        )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nannotation_spine_df = pd.DataFrame(\n    annotation_spine_records\n)\n\nbatch_spine_df = pd.DataFrame(\n    batch_spine_records\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"SPINE TARGET AUDIT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Total filament annotations:\", len(annotations_list))\nprint(\"Valid spines:\", valid_spines)\nprint(\"Missing spines:\", missing_spines)\nprint(\"Malformed/degenerate spines:\", len(invalid_spines))\nprint(\"Annotations with out-of-bounds coordinates:\",\n      out_of_bounds_spines)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Spine Band Statistics ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    batch_spine_df[\n        [\n            \"spine_pixels\",\n            \"spine_inside_fraction\",\n            \"spine_band_to_foreground_pct\"\n        ]\n    ].describe().round(4)\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nBatches with no rasterized spine:\")\n\ndisplay(\n    batch_spine_df[\n        batch_spine_df[\"spine_pixels\"] == 0\n    ].head(10)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Save results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nannotation_spine_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"annotation_spine_audit.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nbatch_spine_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"batch_spine_audit.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSpine audit saved.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Rasterization and Overlay Interpretation\n\nThe filament polygons are rasterized using pycocotools, preserving\nthe COCO annotation rasterization convention.\n\nThe auxiliary spine targets are rasterized separately using\nOpenCV polylines.\n\nThe foreground coverage is measured using the union of all\nfilament instances within each annotation batch.\n\nAcross physical photographs, the median foreground coverage\nis approximately 0.3064%, and the mean is 0.3520%.\nThe 95th percentile is 0.8035%.\n\nThese statistics demonstrate substantial foreground sparsity,\nwhich motivates careful tile sampling and imbalance-aware losses.\n\nRed denotes the filament mask and cyan denotes the auxiliary\nspine target.\n\n**Key Note**\n\n***create_filament_mask()*** reads the coordinate points from the JSON, reshapes them into $(x, y)$ pairs, and uses cv2.fillPoly to paint a 2D matrix of shape (2048, 2048).\n\n***Class Imbalance***: Notice the printed coverage percentage (usually under 0.5% of the full image). This visually proves why we need to crop images into tiles rather than passing empty space into our neural network!\n\nOverlay Sanity Check: In the rightmost plot, red areas show the exact boundaries where filaments sit, while the cyan lines trace their central spines.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Annotation-Set Agreement Study","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 2C: ANNOTATION-SET AGREEMENT\n# Human-reference consistency diagnostic\n# ============================================================\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom itertools import combinations\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport cv2\n\nfrom scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\nfrom pycocotools import mask as mask_utils\n\n\nMATCH_IOU_THRESHOLD = 0.50\nOVERLAP_GRAPH_THRESHOLD = 0.10\nN_BOOTSTRAP = 2000\nBOOTSTRAP_SEED = 42\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Index annotation batches and physical photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbatch_info = {img[\"id\"]: img for img in images_list}\n\nif len(batch_info) != len(images_list):\n    raise ValueError(\"Duplicate COCO image IDs.\")\n\nannotations_by_batch = defaultdict(list)\n\nfor ann in annotations_list:\n    if ann[\"image_id\"] not in batch_info:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown image ID: {ann['image_id']}\")\n\n    annotations_by_batch[ann[\"image_id\"]].append(ann)\n\nphoto_to_batches = defaultdict(list)\n\nfor img in images_list:\n    photo_to_batches[img[\"file_name\"]].append(img[\"id\"])\n\nmulti_batch_photos = {\n    filename: sorted(batch_ids)\n    for filename, batch_ids in photo_to_batches.items()\n    if len(batch_ids) > 1\n}\n\nprint(\n    \"Physical photographs with multiple annotation sets:\",\n    len(multi_batch_photos)\n)\n\nif not multi_batch_photos:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No multiple-annotation photographs found.\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Convert individual filament polygons into COCO RLEs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef annotation_to_rle(ann, height, width):\n\n    polygons = ann.get(\"segmentation\", [])\n\n    if not polygons:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Empty segmentation: {ann.get('id')}\"\n        )\n\n    polygon_rles = mask_utils.frPyObjects(\n        polygons, height, width\n    )\n\n    if not polygon_rles:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Cannot rasterize: {ann.get('id')}\"\n        )\n\n    return mask_utils.merge(polygon_rles)\n\n\ndef build_batch_targets(batch_id):\n\n    info = batch_info[batch_id]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    instance_rles = [\n        annotation_to_rle(ann, h, w)\n        for ann in annotations_by_batch.get(batch_id, [])\n    ]\n\n    if instance_rles:\n        semantic_rle = mask_utils.merge(instance_rles)\n    else:\n        empty = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=np.uint8, order=\"F\")\n\n        semantic_rle = mask_utils.encode(\n            np.asfortranarray(empty)\n        )\n\n    return {\n        \"height\": h,\n        \"width\": w,\n        \"instance_rles\": instance_rles,\n        \"semantic_rle\": semantic_rle\n    }\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Semantic foreground agreement\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef semantic_dice_iou(rle_a, rle_b):\n\n    area_a = float(mask_utils.area(rle_a))\n    area_b = float(mask_utils.area(rle_b))\n\n    if area_a == 0 and area_b == 0:\n        return 1.0, 1.0\n\n    iou = float(\n        mask_utils.iou(\n            [rle_a],\n            [rle_b],\n            [0]\n        )[0, 0]\n    )\n\n    dice = (\n        2.0 * iou / (1.0 + iou)\n        if iou > 0 else 0.0\n    )\n\n    return dice, iou\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. One-to-one instance matching\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef calculate_instance_agreement(rles_a, rles_b):\n\n    n_a = len(rles_a)\n    n_b = len(rles_b)\n\n    if n_a and n_b:\n\n        iou_matrix = np.asarray(\n            mask_utils.iou(\n                rles_a,\n                rles_b,\n                [0] * n_b\n            ),\n            dtype=np.float64\n        )\n\n    else:\n\n        iou_matrix = np.zeros(\n            (n_a, n_b),\n            dtype=np.float64\n        )\n\n    valid = iou_matrix > MATCH_IOU_THRESHOLD\n\n    if n_a and n_b:\n\n        # Lexicographic optimization:\n        # first maximize the number of valid matches;\n        # then maximize their total IoU.\n\n        bonus = min(n_a, n_b) + 1.0\n\n        weights = np.where(\n            valid,\n            bonus + iou_matrix,\n            0.0\n        )\n\n        row_idx, col_idx = linear_sum_assignment(\n            -weights\n        )\n\n        matches = [\n            (i, j, float(iou_matrix[i, j]))\n            for i, j in zip(row_idx, col_idx)\n            if valid[i, j]\n        ]\n\n    else:\n\n        matches = []\n\n    tp = len(matches)\n    fp = n_b - tp\n    fn = n_a - tp\n\n    denominator = tp + 0.5 * fp + 0.5 * fn\n\n    sum_iou = sum(\n        score for _, _, score in matches\n    )\n\n    if denominator == 0:\n        pq = 1.0\n        rq = 1.0\n    else:\n        pq = sum_iou / denominator\n        rq = tp / denominator\n\n    sq = (\n        sum_iou / tp\n        if tp else np.nan\n    )\n\n    matched_dice = [\n        2.0 * score / (1.0 + score)\n        for _, _, score in matches\n    ]\n\n    mean_matched_dice = (\n        float(np.mean(matched_dice))\n        if matched_dice else np.nan\n    )\n\n    # Exploratory overlap relationships.\n    # These are not official competition fragmentation counts.\n\n    overlap_graph = (\n        iou_matrix >= OVERLAP_GRAPH_THRESHOLD\n    )\n\n    a_overlaps_multiple_b = int(\n        np.sum(overlap_graph.sum(axis=1) >= 2)\n    )\n\n    b_overlaps_multiple_a = int(\n        np.sum(overlap_graph.sum(axis=0) >= 2)\n    )\n\n    return {\n        \"TP\": tp,\n        \"FP\": fp,\n        \"FN\": fn,\n        \"PQ_style\": float(pq),\n        \"SQ\": float(sq) if np.isfinite(sq) else np.nan,\n        \"RQ\": float(rq),\n        \"mean_matched_instance_dice\": mean_matched_dice,\n        \"A_instances_overlapping_multiple_B_iou_ge_0p1\":\n            a_overlaps_multiple_b,\n        \"B_instances_overlapping_multiple_A_iou_ge_0p1\":\n            b_overlaps_multiple_a\n    }\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Compare all annotation-set pairs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\npair_rows = []\n\nfor photo_idx, (file_name, batch_ids) in enumerate(\n    sorted(multi_batch_photos.items()),\n    start=1\n):\n\n    # Cache only one physical photo at a time.\n    targets = {\n        batch_id: build_batch_targets(batch_id)\n        for batch_id in batch_ids\n    }\n\n    dimensions = {\n        (target[\"height\"], target[\"width\"])\n        for target in targets.values()\n    }\n\n    if len(dimensions) != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Inconsistent dimensions: {file_name}\"\n        )\n\n    for batch_a, batch_b in combinations(batch_ids, 2):\n\n        target_a = targets[batch_a]\n        target_b = targets[batch_b]\n\n        sem_dice, sem_iou = semantic_dice_iou(\n            target_a[\"semantic_rle\"],\n            target_b[\"semantic_rle\"]\n        )\n\n        inst = calculate_instance_agreement(\n            target_a[\"instance_rles\"],\n            target_b[\"instance_rles\"]\n        )\n\n        pair_rows.append({\n\n            \"file_name\": file_name,\n            \"batch_A\": batch_a,\n            \"batch_B\": batch_b,\n\n            \"site_code\": Path(file_name).stem[-2:],\n\n            \"instances_A\": len(\n                target_a[\"instance_rles\"]\n            ),\n\n            \"instances_B\": len(\n                target_b[\"instance_rles\"]\n            ),\n\n            \"instance_count_difference\": abs(\n                len(target_a[\"instance_rles\"])\n                - len(target_b[\"instance_rles\"])\n            ),\n\n            \"semantic_dice\": sem_dice,\n            \"semantic_iou\": sem_iou,\n\n            **inst\n        })\n\n    if photo_idx % 50 == 0:\n        print(\n            f\"Compared {photo_idx}/\"\n            f\"{len(multi_batch_photos)} photographs\"\n        )\n\n\npair_agreement_df = pd.DataFrame(pair_rows)\n\nif pair_agreement_df.empty:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No annotation-set comparisons generated.\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Aggregate pairs within each physical photo\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nmetric_columns = [\n    \"semantic_dice\",\n    \"semantic_iou\",\n    \"PQ_style\",\n    \"SQ\",\n    \"RQ\",\n    \"mean_matched_instance_dice\"\n]\n\nphoto_agreement_df = (\n    pair_agreement_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[metric_columns]\n    .mean()\n    .reset_index()\n)\n\npair_counts = (\n    pair_agreement_df.groupby(\"file_name\")\n    .size()\n    .rename(\"n_pairs\")\n    .reset_index()\n)\n\nphoto_agreement_df = photo_agreement_df.merge(\n    pair_counts,\n    on=\"file_name\",\n    validate=\"one_to_one\"\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7. Bootstrap CI across physical photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef bootstrap_mean_ci(\n    values,\n    n_boot=N_BOOTSTRAP,\n    seed=BOOTSTRAP_SEED\n):\n\n    values = np.asarray(\n        values, dtype=np.float64\n    )\n\n    values = values[np.isfinite(values)]\n\n    if values.size == 0:\n        return np.nan, np.nan\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n\n    indices = rng.integers(\n        0,\n        values.size,\n        size=(n_boot, values.size)\n    )\n\n    bootstrap_means = values[indices].mean(axis=1)\n\n    return tuple(\n        float(x)\n        for x in np.quantile(\n            bootstrap_means, [0.025, 0.975]\n        )\n    )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Report results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"ANNOTATION-SET AGREEMENT RESULTS\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\n    \"Physical photographs compared:\",\n    len(photo_agreement_df)\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Total pair comparisons:\",\n    len(pair_agreement_df)\n)\n\nfor metric in metric_columns:\n\n    values = photo_agreement_df[metric].dropna().to_numpy()\n\n    lo, hi = bootstrap_mean_ci(values)\n\n    print(f\"\\n{metric}\")\n\n    print(\"Physical photos:\", len(values))\n    print(f\"Mean:   {np.mean(values):.4f}\")\n    print(f\"Median: {np.median(values):.4f}\")\n\n    if len(values) > 1:\n        print(f\"SD:     {np.std(values, ddof=1):.4f}\")\n\n    print(\n        f\"95% photo-bootstrap CI: \"\n        f\"[{lo:.4f}, {hi:.4f}]\"\n    )\n\n\nprint(\"\\nInstance-count difference:\")\n\ndisplay(\n    pair_agreement_df[\n        \"instance_count_difference\"\n    ].describe().round(3)\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Report lowest agreement and diagnose zero-Dice pairs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\nLowest semantic-agreement photographs:\")\n\ndisplay(\n    photo_agreement_df.sort_values(\n        \"semantic_dice\"\n    ).head(10)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Investigate complete semantic disagreements\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nzero_cases = pair_agreement_df[\n    pair_agreement_df[\"semantic_dice\"] <= 1e-12\n].copy()\n\nprint(\n    \"\\nCompletely disjoint annotation-set pairs:\",\n    len(zero_cases)\n)\n\nfor _, row in zero_cases.iterrows():\n\n    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\n    print(\"Physical photograph:\", row[\"file_name\"])\n    print(\"Semantic Dice:\", row[\"semantic_dice\"])\n\n    batch_a = row[\"batch_A\"]\n    batch_b = row[\"batch_B\"]\n\n    target_a = build_batch_targets(batch_a)\n    target_b = build_batch_targets(batch_b)\n\n    area_a = int(\n        mask_utils.area(target_a[\"semantic_rle\"])\n    )\n\n    area_b = int(\n        mask_utils.area(target_b[\"semantic_rle\"])\n    )\n\n    union_rle = mask_utils.merge([\n        target_a[\"semantic_rle\"],\n        target_b[\"semantic_rle\"]\n    ])\n\n    union_area = int(\n        mask_utils.area(union_rle)\n    )\n\n    intersection_area = area_a + area_b - union_area\n\n    print(\"\\nBatch A:\", batch_a)\n    print(\"Number of filaments:\", len(target_a[\"instance_rles\"]))\n    print(\"Semantic foreground pixels:\", area_a)\n\n    anns_a = annotations_by_batch.get(batch_a, [])\n\n    print(\n        \"Individual filament areas:\",\n        [int(round(float(a[\"area\"]))) for a in anns_a]\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nBatch B:\", batch_b)\n    print(\"Number of filaments:\", len(target_b[\"instance_rles\"]))\n    print(\"Semantic foreground pixels:\", area_b)\n\n    anns_b = annotations_by_batch.get(batch_b, [])\n\n    print(\n        \"Individual filament areas:\",\n        [int(round(float(a[\"area\"]))) for a in anns_b]\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nIntersection pixels:\", intersection_area)\n    print(\"Combined union pixels:\", union_area)\n\n    if area_a == 0 and area_b == 0:\n\n        print(\"DIAGNOSIS: Both annotation sets are empty.\")\n\n    elif area_a == 0 or area_b == 0:\n\n        print(\"DIAGNOSIS: One annotation set has no foreground.\")\n\n    elif intersection_area == 0:\n\n        print(\n            \"DIAGNOSIS: Both sets contain foreground, \"\n            \"but their semantic masks are completely disjoint.\"\n        )\n\n    else:\n\n        print(\n            \"DIAGNOSIS: Check Dice computation and \"\n            \"mask consistency; intersection is non-zero.\"\n        )\n\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 9. Save results\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)\n\npair_agreement_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"annotation_set_pair_agreement.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nphoto_agreement_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"annotation_set_photo_agreement.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSaved:\")\nprint(\"annotation_set_pair_agreement.csv\")\nprint(\"annotation_set_photo_agreement.csv\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 10. Visualize four lowest-agreement physical photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nworst_photo_names = (\n    photo_agreement_df.nsmallest(\n        min(4, len(photo_agreement_df)),\n        \"semantic_dice\"\n    )[\"file_name\"].tolist()\n)\n\n# One pair per physical photo, avoiding duplicate images.\nworst_pairs = (\n    pair_agreement_df[\n        pair_agreement_df[\"file_name\"].isin(worst_photo_names)\n    ]\n    .sort_values(\"semantic_dice\")\n    .groupby(\"file_name\", as_index=False)\n    .first()\n)\n\n\ndef semantic_mask_for_batch(batch_id):\n\n    target = build_batch_targets(batch_id)\n\n    return mask_utils.decode(\n        target[\"semantic_rle\"]\n    ).astype(bool)\n\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(\n    len(worst_pairs),\n    2,\n    figsize=(14, 4 * len(worst_pairs)),\n    squeeze=False\n)\n\nfor row_idx, (_, record) in enumerate(\n    worst_pairs.iterrows()\n):\n\n    file_name = record[\"file_name\"]\n\n    image = cv2.imread(\n        str(TRAIN_IMG_DIR / file_name),\n        cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n    )\n\n    if image is None:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(file_name)\n\n    mask_a = semantic_mask_for_batch(record[\"batch_A\"])\n    mask_b = semantic_mask_for_batch(record[\"batch_B\"])\n\n    if mask_a.shape != image.shape or mask_b.shape != image.shape:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Shape mismatch: {file_name}\")\n\n    rgb = cv2.cvtColor(\n        image, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB\n    )\n\n    overlay = rgb.copy()\n\n    a_only = mask_a & ~mask_b\n    b_only = mask_b & ~mask_a\n    common = mask_a & mask_b\n\n    overlay[a_only] = (255, 60, 60)\n    overlay[b_only] = (50, 220, 255)\n    overlay[common] = (255, 225, 0)\n\n    axes[row_idx, 0].imshow(image, cmap=\"gray\")\n    axes[row_idx, 0].set_title(file_name)\n    axes[row_idx, 0].axis(\"off\")\n\n    axes[row_idx, 1].imshow(overlay)\n    axes[row_idx, 1].set_title(\n        f\"Red: A only | Cyan: B only | Yellow: overlap\\n\"\n        f\"Semantic Dice={record['semantic_dice']:.3f}; \"\n        f\"PQ-style={record['PQ_style']:.3f}\"\n    )\n    axes[row_idx, 1].axis(\"off\")\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Scientific interpretation of this experiment:**\n\n- Semantic Dice measures agreement between the union of filament masks.\n- PQ-style agreement uses one-to-one matching with IoU greater than 0.5.\n- SQ is conditional on having matched instances.\n- The bootstrap resamples physical photographs, not individual pair comparisons. This prevents photographs with three annotation sets from receiving disproportionate statistical weight.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Ingestion and Utility Pipeline Setup\n\nWhen our model makes predictions at inference time, we cannot submit raw $2048 \\times 2048$ image files. Kaggle expects a CSV containing Run-Length Encoded (RLE) strings for every detected instance.\n\n**Lossless Roundtripping Verification**: A simple 1-pixel shift or transposing $(x, y) \\to (y, x)$ in our RLE encoder will silently reduce the model's score. This cell builds the encoder/decoder functions using pycocotools and performs a unit test to guarantee $100\\%$ lossless roundtripping.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import numpy as np\nfrom pycocotools import mask as mask_utils","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Binary Mask <--> RLE String interconverter","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def mask_to_rle(binary_mask):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a 2D binary numpy array (uint8, 0 or 1) into a COCO/Kaggle standard RLE string.\n    Fortran order ('F') is required by pycocotools to match column-major standards.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(binary_mask, np.ndarray):\n        binary_mask = np.array(binary_mask)\n        \n    # Ensure binary uint8 format\n    binary_mask = (binary_mask > 0).astype(np.uint8)\n    \n    # pycocotools expects Fortran-contiguous array (column-major order)\n    fortran_mask = np.asfortranarray(binary_mask)\n    rle = mask_utils.encode(fortran_mask)\n    \n    # Decode byte string to standard UTF-8 string for CSV export\n    rle[\"counts\"] = rle[\"counts\"].decode(\"utf-8\")\n    return rle\n\ndef rle_to_mask(rle_dict, height=2048, width=2048):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes an RLE dictionary/string back into a 2D binary numpy array (height, width).\n    \"\"\"\n    # If passed as raw string/counts dict, structure correctly for pycocotools\n    if isinstance(rle_dict, str):\n        rle_dict = {\"size\": [height, width], \"counts\": rle_dict.encode(\"utf-8\")}\n    elif isinstance(rle_dict, dict) and isinstance(rle_dict[\"counts\"], str):\n        rle_dict = rle_dict.copy()\n        rle_dict[\"counts\"] = rle_dict[\"counts\"].encode(\"utf-8\")\n        \n    binary_mask = mask_utils.decode(rle_dict)\n    return binary_mask.astype(np.uint8)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Sample test of the Mask <-> RLE encoder/decoder on sample image","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"--- Running RLE Roundtrip Verification Test ---\")\n\n# Pick the first individual instance mask from our previous work\ntest_instance = inst_masks[0]\n\n# 1. Encode mask to RLE\nencoded_rle = mask_to_rle(test_instance)\n\n# 2. Decode RLE back to mask\ndecoded_mask = rle_to_mask(encoded_rle, height=2048, width=2048)\n\n# 3. Check exact equality across all 4.19 million pixels\nis_identical = np.array_equal(test_instance, decoded_mask)\ncompression_ratio = (len(str(encoded_rle[\"counts\"])) / (2048 * 2048)) * 100\n\nprint(f\"Original Mask Shape:   {test_instance.shape}\")\nprint(f\"RLE Compact Output:   {str(encoded_rle['counts'])[:60]}...\")\nprint(f\"Compression Efficiency: {compression_ratio:.5f}% of original pixel size\")\nprint(f\"Lossless Match Check:  {'✅ PASSED (100% Match)' if is_identical else '❌ FAILED (Mismatch Found)'}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Grid Tiling, Filtering & Patch Reconstruction Engine","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## Grid Tiling, Sampling and Reconstruction\n\nThe original observations are 2048 × 2048 pixels.\n\nWe use 512 × 512 tiles to retain the original pixel sampling\nwhile reducing GPU memory requirements.\n\nA stride of 384 pixels introduces 128 pixels of overlap between\nadjacent tiles. This reduces the likelihood of truncating\nstructures at tile boundaries.\n\nTraining will include:\n- Tiles containing at least one filament pixel.\n- A controlled sample of background-only tiles.\n\nWe will measure the actual positive-to-negative tile ratio\nrather than assuming a fixed proportion.\n\nAt inference, all image tiles will be processed and their\npredicted probability maps blended into the original image\ncoordinate system.\n\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n    \n```\nFULL SOLAR DISK (2048 x 2048)                    GRID OF 512 x 512 TILES\n┌───────────────────────────────────┐        ┌───────┬───────┬───────┬───────┐\n│                                   │        │Tile 1 │Tile 2 │Tile 3 │Tile 4 │\n│            .──.                   │        ├───────┼───────┼───────┼───────┤\n│           (    )  ◄── Filament    │  ──►   │Tile 5 │Tile 6 │Tile 7 │Tile 8 │\n│            `──'                   │        ├───────┼───────┼───────┼───────┤\n│                                   │        │Tile 9 │Tile 10│Tile 11│Tile 12│\n│                                   │        ├───────┼───────┼───────┼───────┤\n│                                   │        │Tile 13│Tile 14│Tile 15│Tile 16│\n└───────────────────────────────────┘        └───────┴───────┴───────┴───────┘\n```\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Tile Extraction Function (For Training & Feature Prep)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def extract_tiles(image, mask, spine_mask=None, tile_size=512, stride=384, min_filament_pixels=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a 2048x2048 image and mask into tile_size x tile_size patches.\n    \n    Args:\n        image: (H, W) or (H, W, C) numpy array\n        mask: (H, W) binary mask array\n        spine_mask: (H, W) spine mask array (optional)\n        tile_size: Height/Width of square tiles (default 512)\n        stride: Step size between tiles (stride < tile_size creates overlap)\n        min_filament_pixels: Minimum positive mask pixels required to keep a tile.\n                            Set to 0 to keep all tiles (useful for inference).\n    \n    Returns:\n        tiles_dict: List of dicts containing image_patch, mask_patch, spine_patch, (y, x) coords\n    \"\"\"\n    h, w = image.shape[:2]\n    tiles = []\n\n    # Calculate top-left starting positions for sliding window\n    y_steps = list(range(0, h - tile_size + 1, stride))\n    x_steps = list(range(0, w - tile_size + 1, stride))\n    \n    # Ensure edge boundaries cover the entire image\n    if y_steps[-1] + tile_size < h:\n        y_steps.append(h - tile_size)\n    if x_steps[-1] + tile_size < w:\n        x_steps.append(w - tile_size)\n\n    for y in y_steps:\n        for x in x_steps:\n            img_tile = image[y:y+tile_size, x:x+tile_size]\n            mask_tile = mask[y:y+tile_size, x:x+tile_size]\n            spine_tile = spine_mask[y:y+tile_size, x:x+tile_size] if spine_mask is not None else None\n            \n            filament_pixel_count = np.sum(mask_tile > 0)\n            \n            # Keep tile if it passes minimum pixel threshold\n            if filament_pixel_count >= min_filament_pixels:\n                tiles.append({\n                    \"img_tile\": img_tile,\n                    \"mask_tile\": mask_tile,\n                    \"spine_tile\": spine_tile,\n                    \"coords\": (y, x, tile_size, tile_size),\n                    \"pixel_count\": filament_pixel_count\n                })\n\n    return tiles","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Tile Reconstruction Function (Stitches Tiles back into 2048x2048)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def reconstruct_from_tiles(tiles, full_shape=(2048, 2048)):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reconstructs full-resolution predictions from predicted tile patches,\n    using linear accumulation to smoothly average overlapping tile borders.\n    \"\"\"\n    reconstructed_mask = np.zeros(full_shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    weight_map = np.zeros(full_shape, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for tile_info in tiles:\n        y, x, h, w = tile_info[\"coords\"]\n        pred_patch = tile_info[\"mask_tile\"]\n\n        reconstructed_mask[y:y+h, x:x+w] += pred_patch\n        weight_map[y:y+h, x:x+w] += 1.0\n\n    # Avoid division by zero in untouched background areas\n    weight_map = np.maximum(weight_map, 1.0)\n    averaged_mask = reconstructed_mask / weight_map\n    \n    return averaged_mask","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Verification of The Tile Extraction, Reconstruction Pipeline","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# TILE EXTRACTION / RECONSTRUCTION SANITY CHECK\n# ============================================================\n\nTILE_SIZE = 512\nTILE_STRIDE = 384\n\nall_overlapping_tiles = extract_tiles(\n    raw_img,\n    combined_mask,\n    spine_mask,\n    tile_size=TILE_SIZE,\n    stride=TILE_STRIDE,\n    min_filament_pixels=0\n)\n\n# Preserve even tiles containing just one foreground pixel.\npositive_tiles = [\n    tile for tile in all_overlapping_tiles\n    if tile[\"pixel_count\"] >= 1\n]\n\nnegative_tiles = [\n    tile for tile in all_overlapping_tiles\n    if tile[\"pixel_count\"] == 0\n]\n\n# Verify full spatial coverage.\ncoverage_count = np.zeros(\n    combined_mask.shape,\n    dtype=np.uint16\n)\n\nfor tile in all_overlapping_tiles:\n    y, x, h, w = tile[\"coords\"]\n    coverage_count[y:y+h, x:x+w] += 1\n\nassert np.all(coverage_count > 0), (\n    \"Tile grid leaves uncovered pixels.\"\n)\n\nassert np.all(coverage_count[combined_mask > 0] > 0), (\n    \"Some filament pixels are not covered.\"\n)\n\n# Test reconstruction using the same overlapping grid.\nreconstructed = reconstruct_from_tiles(\n    all_overlapping_tiles,\n    full_shape=combined_mask.shape\n)\n\nmax_error = float(\n    np.max(\n        np.abs(\n            combined_mask.astype(np.float32) - reconstructed\n        )\n    )\n)\n\nassert max_error <= 1e-6, (\n    f\"Reconstruction failed: {max_error}\"\n)\n\nprint(\"Total overlapping tiles:\", len(all_overlapping_tiles))\nprint(\"Positive tiles:\", len(positive_tiles))\nprint(\"Negative tiles:\", len(negative_tiles))\nprint(\"Foreground pixels:\", int(combined_mask.sum()))\nprint(\"Minimum coverage:\", int(coverage_count.min()))\nprint(\"Maximum reconstruction error:\", max_error)\nprint(\"Tile reconstruction: PASSED\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual Analysis ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"num_samples = min(4, len(positive_tiles))\nif num_samples > 0:\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, num_samples, figsize=(4 * num_samples, 8))\n    \n    for i in range(num_samples):\n        tile_data = positive_tiles[i]\n        y, x, h, w = tile_data[\"coords\"]\n        \n        # Row 1: Image Tile\n        axes[0, i].imshow(tile_data[\"img_tile\"], cmap=\"gray\")\n        axes[0, i].set_title(f\"Tile {i+1} Image\\nCoords: ({y}, {x})\")\n        axes[0, i].axis(\"off\")\n        \n        # Row 2: Filament Mask Tile\n        axes[1, i].imshow(tile_data[\"mask_tile\"], cmap=\"magma\")\n        axes[1, i].set_title(f\"Filament Mask\\nPixels: {tile_data['pixel_count']}\")\n        axes[1, i].axis(\"off\")\n\n    plt.suptitle(\"Sample 512x512 Extracted Training Tiles (Positive Filaments)\", fontsize=14, y=1.02)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## Exploratory Morphological Characterization\n\nThe analysis describes filament area, spine length, centroid\ndistribution, annotation counts and geometric ratios.\n\nBounding-box aspect ratio provides a coarse shape descriptor.\nSpine length and area-to-spine-length ratio offer additional\ndescriptive information for curved filament structures.\n\nThese measurements motivate experiments with topology-aware\nlosses such as clDice. They do not establish that such losses\nwill improve segmentation performance.\n\nSpatial density is reported in detector-image coordinates.\nHeliographic interpretation requires additional solar geometry.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Metadata Extraction & Distribution Analysis","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# sample\nannotations_list[:3]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Annotation geometry and foreground characterization\n\nNow comes a scientifically important part: understanding what the model will actually learn.\n\nWe have 8,199 annotated filament instances. We need to characterize their geometry before selecting our network architecture, tile size and loss functions.\n\nThis cell calculates polygon centroids using the shoelace formula, measures spine length, estimates mean width, verifies stored COCO areas for all 8,199 annotations, and measures the actual union coverage for every annotation batch.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# STAGE 2B: FILAMENT GEOMETRY AND ANNOTATION CHARACTERIZATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom pycocotools import mask as mask_utils\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\nplt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 11})\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Metadata mappings\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img for img in images_list\n}\n\nimage_id_to_file = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img[\"file_name\"] for img in images_list\n}\n\ncat_id_to_name = {\n    cat[\"id\"]: cat[\"name\"] for cat in categories_list\n}\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Polygon geometry using the shoelace formula\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef calculate_polygon_geometry(segmentation):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates area and area-weighted centroid of COCO polygons.\n\n    The centroid is calculated from polygon coordinates,\n    NOT from the bounding box.\n\n    Supports multiple polygons defensively.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    total_area = 0.0\n    weighted_x = 0.0\n    weighted_y = 0.0\n\n    for polygon in segmentation:\n\n        coords = np.asarray(\n            polygon, dtype=np.float64\n        )\n\n        if (\n            coords.ndim != 1\n            or coords.size < 6\n            or coords.size % 2 != 0\n            or not np.isfinite(coords).all()\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid polygon coordinates.\")\n\n        points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n        # Remove repeated closing vertex, if present\n        if np.allclose(points[0], points[-1]):\n            points = points[:-1]\n\n        if len(points) < 3:\n            raise ValueError(\"Polygon has fewer than 3 vertices.\")\n\n        x = points[:, 0]\n        y = points[:, 1]\n\n        x_next = np.roll(x, -1)\n        y_next = np.roll(y, -1)\n\n        cross = x * y_next - x_next * y\n\n        signed_area = 0.5 * np.sum(cross)\n        polygon_area = abs(signed_area)\n\n        if polygon_area <= 1e-10:\n            raise ValueError(\"Degenerate polygon.\")\n\n        cx = np.sum((x + x_next) * cross) / (\n            6.0 * signed_area\n        )\n\n        cy = np.sum((y + y_next) * cross) / (\n            6.0 * signed_area\n        )\n\n        total_area += polygon_area\n        weighted_x += polygon_area * cx\n        weighted_y += polygon_area * cy\n\n    if total_area <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty polygon geometry.\")\n\n    return (\n        total_area,\n        weighted_x / total_area,\n        weighted_y / total_area\n    )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Calculate spine length\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef calculate_spine_length(spine):\n\n    if not spine or len(spine) < 4:\n        return np.nan, 0\n\n    coords = np.asarray(spine, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    if (\n        coords.ndim != 1\n        or coords.size % 2 != 0\n        or not np.isfinite(coords).all()\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid spine coordinates.\")\n\n    points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    differences = np.diff(points, axis=0)\n\n    segment_lengths = np.sqrt(\n        np.sum(differences ** 2, axis=1)\n    )\n\n    return float(segment_lengths.sum()), len(points)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Extract one record per filament\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nrecords = []\n\ninvalid_geometry = []\n\nfor ann in annotations_list:\n\n    image_info = image_info_by_id[ann[\"image_id\"]]\n\n    segmentation = ann.get(\"segmentation\", [])\n\n    bbox = np.asarray(\n        ann.get(\"bbox\", []),\n        dtype=np.float64\n    )\n\n    try:\n\n        polygon_area, centroid_x, centroid_y = (\n            calculate_polygon_geometry(segmentation)\n        )\n\n        spine_length, spine_points = (\n            calculate_spine_length(ann.get(\"spine\", []))\n        )\n\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\n\n        invalid_geometry.append(\n            (ann[\"id\"], str(exc))\n        )\n\n        continue\n\n    if (\n        bbox.size != 4\n        or not np.isfinite(bbox).all()\n        or bbox[2] < 0\n        or bbox[3] < 0\n    ):\n        invalid_geometry.append(\n            (ann[\"id\"], \"Invalid bounding box\")\n        )\n        continue\n\n    x, y, w, h = bbox\n\n    stored_area = float(ann[\"area\"])\n\n    # Area / spine length: approximate mean transverse width\n    # This is a geometric proxy, not a direct width measurement.\n    width_proxy = (\n        stored_area / spine_length\n        if np.isfinite(spine_length) and spine_length > 0\n        else np.nan\n    )\n\n    # Spine length / width proxy\n    elongation_proxy = (\n        spine_length / width_proxy\n        if np.isfinite(width_proxy) and width_proxy > 0\n        else np.nan\n    )\n\n    aspect_ratio = (\n        max(w, h) / max(min(w, h), 1.0)\n    )\n\n    file_name = image_info[\"file_name\"]\n\n    records.append({\n\n        \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n        \"image_id\": ann[\"image_id\"],\n        \"file_name\": file_name,\n\n        \"site_code\": Path(file_name).stem[-2:],\n\n        \"category_id\": ann[\"category_id\"],\n        \"category_name\": cat_id_to_name.get(\n            ann[\"category_id\"], \"Unknown\"\n        ),\n\n        \"area\": stored_area,\n        \"polygon_geometry_area\": polygon_area,\n\n        \"bbox_w\": w,\n        \"bbox_h\": h,\n        \"bbox_aspect_ratio\": aspect_ratio,\n\n        \"centroid_x\": centroid_x,\n        \"centroid_y\": centroid_y,\n\n        \"spine_length_px\": spine_length,\n        \"num_spine_points\": spine_points,\n\n        \"width_proxy_px\": width_proxy,\n        \"spine_elongation_proxy\": elongation_proxy,\n\n        \"n_batches_for_photo\": len(\n            physical_file_to_image_ids.get(file_name, [])\n        )\n    })\n\n\ndf_eda = pd.DataFrame(records)\n\nif df_eda.empty:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No valid filament records were generated.\")\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"FILAMENT INSTANCE CHARACTERIZATION\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Valid instances:\", len(df_eda))\nprint(\"Invalid geometry:\", len(invalid_geometry))\nprint(\"Physical photographs:\", df_eda[\"file_name\"].nunique())\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", df_eda[\"image_id\"].nunique())\n\nprint(\"\\nFirst five records:\")\ndisplay(df_eda.head())\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Verify all COCO annotation areas using pycocotools\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbatch_instance_rles = defaultdict(list)\n\narea_errors = []\n\nfor ann in annotations_list:\n\n    image_info = image_info_by_id[ann[\"image_id\"]]\n\n    h = int(image_info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(image_info[\"width\"])\n\n    polygon_rles = mask_utils.frPyObjects(\n        ann[\"segmentation\"], h, w\n    )\n\n    # One independent RLE per annotated filament\n    instance_rle = mask_utils.merge(polygon_rles)\n\n    rasterized_area = float(\n        mask_utils.area(instance_rle)\n    )\n\n    stored_area = float(ann[\"area\"])\n\n    area_errors.append(\n        abs(rasterized_area - stored_area)\n    )\n\n    batch_instance_rles[ann[\"image_id\"]].append(\n        instance_rle\n    )\n\n\narea_errors = np.asarray(area_errors)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"FULL-DATASET COCO AREA VERIFICATION\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Annotations checked:\", len(area_errors))\nprint(\"Maximum area discrepancy:\", area_errors.max())\nprint(\"Mean area discrepancy:\", area_errors.mean())\nprint(\"Annotations with non-zero discrepancy:\",\n      int(np.count_nonzero(area_errors)))\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Measure foreground coverage per annotation batch\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbatch_records = []\n\nfor image_info in images_list:\n\n    image_id = image_info[\"id\"]\n    file_name = image_info[\"file_name\"]\n\n    h = int(image_info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(image_info[\"width\"])\n\n    annotations = image_id_to_anns[image_id]\n\n    instance_rles = batch_instance_rles.get(image_id, [])\n\n    if instance_rles:\n\n        # Merge instances so overlapping pixels are counted once\n        union_rle = mask_utils.merge(instance_rles)\n\n        union_area = float(\n            mask_utils.area(union_rle)\n        )\n\n    else:\n        union_area = 0.0\n\n    total_instance_area = sum(\n        float(ann[\"area\"]) for ann in annotations\n    )\n\n    overlap_excess = total_instance_area - union_area\n\n    batch_records.append({\n\n        \"image_id\": image_id,\n        \"file_name\": file_name,\n        \"site_code\": Path(file_name).stem[-2:],\n\n        \"n_instances\": len(annotations),\n\n        \"union_area_px\": union_area,\n\n        \"sum_instance_area_px\": total_instance_area,\n\n        \"overlap_excess_px\": overlap_excess,\n\n        \"union_coverage_pct\": (\n            100.0 * union_area / (h * w)\n        )\n    })\n\n\nbatch_coverage_df = pd.DataFrame(batch_records)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7. Aggregate multiple annotation batches per physical photo\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphoto_coverage_df = (\n\n    batch_coverage_df.groupby(\"file_name\")\n\n    .agg(\n\n        site_code=(\"site_code\", \"first\"),\n\n        n_batches=(\"image_id\", \"nunique\"),\n\n        median_instances=(\"n_instances\", \"median\"),\n\n        median_foreground_pct=(\n            \"union_coverage_pct\", \"median\"\n        ),\n\n        min_foreground_pct=(\n            \"union_coverage_pct\", \"min\"\n        ),\n\n        max_foreground_pct=(\n            \"union_coverage_pct\", \"max\"\n        )\n\n    )\n\n    .reset_index()\n)\n\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"FOREGROUND COVERAGE\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Physical photographs:\", len(photo_coverage_df))\n\nprint(\n    \"Median coverage across physical photographs:\",\n    f\"{photo_coverage_df['median_foreground_pct'].median():.4f}%\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Mean coverage across physical photographs:\",\n    f\"{photo_coverage_df['median_foreground_pct'].mean():.4f}%\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"95th percentile coverage:\",\n    f\"{photo_coverage_df['median_foreground_pct'].quantile(0.95):.4f}%\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Maximum observed coverage:\",\n    f\"{photo_coverage_df['max_foreground_pct'].max():.4f}%\"\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Inspect differences between annotation batches\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nmulti_annotator_photos = photo_coverage_df[\n    photo_coverage_df[\"n_batches\"] > 1\n]\n\nprint(\"\\nPhysical photos with multiple annotation batches:\",\n      len(multi_annotator_photos))\n\nif not multi_annotator_photos.empty:\n\n    display(\n        multi_annotator_photos.sort_values(\n            \"n_batches\", ascending=False\n        ).head(10)\n    )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 9. Save reproducible analytical outputs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)\n\ndf_eda.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"filament_geometry.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nbatch_coverage_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"batch_foreground_coverage.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nphoto_coverage_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"physical_photo_coverage.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSaved:\")\nprint(\" - filament_geometry.csv\")\nprint(\" - batch_foreground_coverage.csv\")\nprint(\" - physical_photo_coverage.csv\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Compute per image instance count\n\nfilaments_per_image = df_eda.groupby(\"image_id\").size()\n\n# Add images with 0 annotations if any exist in images_list\nall_img_ids = [img[\"id\"] for img in images_list]\nzero_filament_imgs = set(all_img_ids) - set(filaments_per_image.index)\nfor img_id in zero_filament_imgs:\n    filaments_per_image[img_id] = 0","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"filaments_per_image","metadata":{"trusted":true,"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visuals","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 2B: UPDATED VISUAL CHARACTERIZATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\nimport numpy as np\n\nfilaments_per_image = df_eda.groupby(\"image_id\").size()\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(\n    2, 3, figsize=(20, 12)\n)\n\n# A. Instance count per annotation batch\nsns.histplot(\n    filaments_per_image,\n    bins=range(\n        int(filaments_per_image.min()),\n        int(filaments_per_image.max()) + 2\n    ),\n    ax=axes[0, 0],\n    color=\"steelblue\"\n)\n\naxes[0, 0].set_title(\n    \"Filament Instances per Annotation Batch\"\n)\naxes[0, 0].set_xlabel(\"Number of Instances\")\n\n\n# B. Filament area\nsns.histplot(\n    data=df_eda,\n    x=\"area\",\n    bins=60,\n    log_scale=True,\n    ax=axes[0, 1],\n    color=\"salmon\"\n)\n\naxes[0, 1].set_title(\n    \"Filament Area Distribution\"\n)\naxes[0, 1].set_xlabel(\"Area (pixels², logarithmic)\")\n\n\n# C. Spine length\nsns.histplot(\n    data=df_eda,\n    x=\"spine_length_px\",\n    bins=50,\n    log_scale=True,\n    ax=axes[0, 2],\n    color=\"seagreen\"\n)\n\naxes[0, 2].set_title(\n    \"Spine Length Distribution\"\n)\naxes[0, 2].set_xlabel(\"Spine Length (pixels, logarithmic)\")\n\n\n# D. Width proxy\nwidth_data = df_eda[\n    df_eda[\"width_proxy_px\"].notna()\n    & (df_eda[\"width_proxy_px\"] > 0)\n]\n\nsns.histplot(\n    data=width_data,\n    x=\"width_proxy_px\",\n    bins=50,\n    log_scale=True,\n    ax=axes[1, 0],\n    color=\"mediumpurple\"\n)\n\naxes[1, 0].set_title(\"Area-to-Spine-Length Ratio (Proxy)\")\naxes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Area / Spine Length (pixels)\")\n\n\n# E. Spine elongation proxy\nelongation_data = df_eda[\n    df_eda[\"spine_elongation_proxy\"].notna()\n    & (df_eda[\"spine_elongation_proxy\"] > 0)\n]\n\nsns.histplot(\n    data=elongation_data,\n    x=\"spine_elongation_proxy\",\n    bins=50,\n    log_scale=True,\n    ax=axes[1, 1],\n    color=\"darkorange\"\n)\n\naxes[1, 1].set_title(\"Spine Length-Squared / Area Proxy\")\naxes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"Spine Length / Width Proxy\")\n\n\n# F. Polygon centroid density in detector coordinates\nhb = axes[1, 2].hexbin(\n    df_eda[\"centroid_x\"],\n    df_eda[\"centroid_y\"],\n    gridsize=40,\n    mincnt=1,\n    cmap=\"YlOrRd\"\n)\n\naxes[1, 2].set_xlim(0, 2048)\naxes[1, 2].set_ylim(2048, 0)\n\naxes[1, 2].set_title(\n    \"Filament Centroid Density\"\n)\n\naxes[1, 2].set_xlabel(\"Detector X (pixels)\")\naxes[1, 2].set_ylabel(\"Detector Y (pixels)\")\n\nfig.colorbar(\n    hb,\n    ax=axes[1, 2],\n    label=\"Instance Count\"\n)\n\nplt.suptitle(\n    \"MAGFiLO: Filament Morphological Characterization\",\n    fontsize=16\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Numerical summary\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"MORPHOLOGICAL SUMMARY\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nfor col in [\n    \"area\",\n    \"spine_length_px\",\n    \"width_proxy_px\",\n    \"spine_elongation_proxy\"\n]:\n\n    print(f\"\\n{col}\")\n\n    print(\n        df_eda[col].describe(\n            percentiles=[0.10, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.90, 0.95]\n        ).round(3)\n    )\n\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Instances per Annotation Batch ---\")\n\nprint(\n    filaments_per_image.describe().round(3)\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Category Distribution ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    df_eda[\"category_name\"].value_counts(\n        normalize=True\n    ).mul(100).round(2).rename(\"percentage\")\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Observatory Distribution ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    df_eda[\"site_code\"]\n    .value_counts()\n    .sort_index()\n    .rename(\"filament_instances\")\n    .to_frame()\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Physical Photograph Distribution by Site ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    photo_coverage_df[\"site_code\"]\n    .value_counts()\n    .sort_index()\n    .rename(\"physical_photos\")\n    .to_frame()\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Foreground Coverage Across Physical Photos ---\")\n\nprint(\n    photo_coverage_df[\"median_foreground_pct\"]\n    .describe(\n        percentiles=[0.10, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.90, 0.95]\n    )\n    .round(4)\n)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## Scientific Interpretation and Limitations of Initial EDA\n\n### 1. Spatial Distribution\n\nThe centroid density map describes filament locations in detector-image coordinates.\n\nIt does not directly establish heliographic latitude or magnetic activity-band structure. Such an interpretation requires solar-disk geometry and coordinate transformations.\n\nSpatial priors will not be imposed on the initial segmentation model.\n\n### 2. Filament Morphology\n\nFilament areas vary considerably, making small-object preservation important.\n\nBounding-box aspect ratio is only a coarse geometric descriptor. Spine length and area-to-spine-length ratio provide additional descriptors of curved filament morphology.\n\nThe latter is an approximate width proxy, not a direct physical width measurement.\n\n### 3. Category Semantics\n\nLeft, Right and Unidentifiable describe chirality annotation categories.\n\nThey are not foreground/background classes and do not directly encode fragmentation, brightness, or morphological complexity.\n\nThe initial segmentation task is binary foreground segmentation with separate filament instances. Chirality will not be used as a model output unless a distinct scientific question justifies it.\n\n### 4. Foreground Sparsity\n\nForeground coverage must be measured using the union of instance masks, rather than summing instance areas, because overlapping instances would otherwise be counted multiple times.\n\nCoverage is calculated separately for each annotation batch. Multiple batches from the same physical observation are summarized at the physical-photo level to avoid overweighting repeated observations.\n\n### 5. Modelling Implications\n\nThe measured area, width proxy, spine length and instance-count distributions will inform:\n\n- Tile sampling and small-filament preservation.\n- Decoder resolution and feature-map design.\n- Foreground loss weighting.\n- Instance separation and topology-aware evaluation.\n\nNo architectural decision is considered validated until tested on leakage-free validation folds.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Chirality Class Breakdown & Image-Level Co-occurrence Matrix\n\nSolar active regions often spawn multiple filaments with aligned chirality (dextral vs. sinistral). This section audits whether images exhibit single-chirality dominance (e.g., an image having exclusively Right filaments) or mixed chirality, helping us design stratified multi-label validation splits.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Pivot Table: Count Categories per Image\nimage_cat_counts = (\n    df_eda.groupby([\"image_id\", \"category_name\"])\n    .size()\n    .unstack(fill_value=0)\n)\n\n# Ensure all 3 categories exist as columns\nfor cat in [\"Left\", \"Right\", \"Unidentifiable\"]:\n    if cat not in image_cat_counts.columns:\n        image_cat_counts[cat] = 0\n\nimage_cat_counts[\"Total_Filaments\"] = image_cat_counts.sum(axis=1)\n\nprint(\"--- Annotation-Batch-Level Chirality Summary ---\")\nprint(f\"Total Evaluated Images: {len(image_cat_counts)}\")\nprint(\"\\nFirst 5 Images Category Breakdown:\")\ndisplay(image_cat_counts.head(5))","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Compute Chirality Dominance Types\ndef classify_image_type(row):\n    has_left = row[\"Left\"] > 0\n    has_right = row[\"Right\"] > 0\n    has_unid = row[\"Unidentifiable\"] > 0\n    \n    if has_left and not has_right:\n        return \"Left Only (+/- Unid)\"\n    elif has_right and not has_left:\n        return \"Right Only (+/- Unid)\"\n    elif has_left and has_right:\n        return \"Mixed (Left & Right)\"\n    elif has_unid and not (has_left or has_right):\n        return \"Unidentifiable Only\"\n    else:\n        return \"Empty / Zero Filaments\"\n\nimage_cat_counts[\"Image_Chirality_Type\"] = image_cat_counts.apply(classify_image_type, axis=1)\n\ntype_distribution = image_cat_counts[\"Image_Chirality_Type\"].value_counts()","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Compute Category Correlation / Co-occurrence\ncorr_matrix = image_cat_counts[[\"Left\", \"Right\", \"Unidentifiable\"]].corr()\n\n# Visualizations: Co-occurrence & Image Type Breakdown\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n\n# --- Plot A: Image-Level Chirality Profiling ---\ncolors = [\"#4C72B0\", \"#DD8452\", \"#55A868\", \"#C44E52\", \"#8172B3\"]\naxes[0].pie(type_distribution, labels=type_distribution.index, autopct=\"%1.1f%%\", \n            startangle=140, colors=colors[:len(type_distribution)], wedgeprops=dict(width=0.4, edgecolor='w'))\naxes[0].set_title(\"Annotation-Batch Chirality Composition\")\n\n# --- Plot B: Category Presence Correlation Matrix ---\nsns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, fmt=\".3f\", cmap=\"coolwarm\", vmin=-1, vmax=1, ax=axes[1], cbar_kws={'label': 'Pearson Correlation'})\naxes[1].set_title(\"Category Co-occurrence Correlation per Image\")\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Summary Insights Printout\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------\nprint(\"\\n--- Key Chirality Insights ---\")\nprint(f\"• Images with Mixed (Left & Right) Filaments: {image_cat_counts['Image_Chirality_Type'].value_counts().get('Mixed (Left & Right)', 0)} ({image_cat_counts['Image_Chirality_Type'].value_counts(normalize=True).get('Mixed (Left & Right)', 0)*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"• Correlation between Left and Right count:   {corr_matrix.loc['Left', 'Right']:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"• Correlation between Unidentifiable & Left:  {corr_matrix.loc['Unidentifiable', 'Left']:.3f}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## Interpretation and Limitations of Chirality Analysis\n\nThe chirality distribution is calculated at the annotation-batch\nlevel, using Left, Right and Unidentifiable labels.\n\nThe previously observed 67.2% mixed-chirality proportion\ntherefore refers to annotation batches, not unique physical\nsolar photographs.\n\nMultiple annotation batches can refer to the same physical\nobservation, so these observations are not statistically\nindependent.\n\nThe Pearson correlations between chirality counts are\ndescriptive associations. They do not establish physical\nindependence or a relationship with active-region complexity.\n\nUnidentifiable describes an inability to assign a chirality\nlabel. It must not be interpreted automatically as low contrast,\nfragmentation or morphological ambiguity.\n\nChirality is not a target class in the present segmentation task.\nThese exploratory statistics are not used to construct the\nvalidation folds.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Authoritative five-fold split","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 3A: AUTHORITATIVE PHYSICAL-PHOTO-LEVEL FOLDS\n# ============================================================\n\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, KFold\n\nN_FOLDS = 5\nSEED = 42\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Count annotations per COCO annotation batch\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbatch_counts = Counter(\n    ann[\"image_id\"] for ann in annotations_list\n)\n\nbatch_df = pd.DataFrame([\n    {\n        \"image_id\": img[\"id\"],\n        \"file_name\": img[\"file_name\"],\n        \"site_code\": Path(img[\"file_name\"]).stem[-2:],\n        \"n_instances\": batch_counts.get(img[\"id\"], 0)\n    }\n    for img in images_list\n])\n\nassert batch_df[\"image_id\"].is_unique\nassert batch_df[\"file_name\"].notna().all()\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Aggregate to one record per physical photograph\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphoto_df = (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\", as_index=False)\n    .agg(\n        site_code=(\"site_code\", \"first\"),\n        n_batches=(\"image_id\", \"nunique\"),\n        median_instances=(\"n_instances\", \"median\"),\n        max_instances=(\"n_instances\", \"max\")\n    )\n    .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nassert len(photo_df) == 707\nassert photo_df[\"file_name\"].is_unique\n\nassert set(photo_df[\"file_name\"]) == {\n    img[\"file_name\"] for img in images_list\n}\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Build stratification labels\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Four approximately equal population bins using median\n# filament count per physical photograph.\n\nranked_counts = photo_df[\n    \"median_instances\"\n].rank(method=\"first\")\n\nphoto_df[\"count_bin\"] = pd.qcut(\n    ranked_counts,\n    q=4,\n    labels=False\n).astype(int)\n\ncandidate_strata = (\n    photo_df[\"site_code\"].astype(str)\n    + \"_Q\"\n    + photo_df[\"count_bin\"].astype(str)\n)\n\ndef strata_valid(labels):\n\n    counts = pd.Series(labels).value_counts()\n\n    return (\n        len(counts) > 1\n        and counts.min() >= N_FOLDS\n    )\n\nif strata_valid(candidate_strata):\n\n    y = candidate_strata\n    strategy = \"Observatory site × instance-count quartile\"\n\nelif strata_valid(photo_df[\"site_code\"]):\n\n    y = photo_df[\"site_code\"]\n    strategy = \"Observatory site\"\n\nelif strata_valid(photo_df[\"count_bin\"]):\n\n    y = photo_df[\"count_bin\"]\n    strategy = \"Instance-count quartile\"\n\nelse:\n\n    y = None\n    strategy = \"Unstratified KFold fallback\"\n\nprint(\"Stratification:\", strategy)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Assign five folds\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphoto_df[\"fold\"] = -1\n\nif y is not None:\n\n    splitter = StratifiedKFold(\n        n_splits=N_FOLDS,\n        shuffle=True,\n        random_state=SEED\n    )\n\n    splits = splitter.split(\n        np.zeros(len(photo_df)),\n        y\n    )\n\nelse:\n\n    splitter = KFold(\n        n_splits=N_FOLDS,\n        shuffle=True,\n        random_state=SEED\n    )\n\n    splits = splitter.split(photo_df)\n\nfor fold, (_, val_idx) in enumerate(splits):\n\n    photo_df.loc[val_idx, \"fold\"] = fold\n\nassert (photo_df[\"fold\"] >= 0).all()\nassert photo_df[\"fold\"].nunique() == N_FOLDS\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Propagate physical-photo folds to annotation batches\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfile_to_fold = dict(\n    zip(photo_df[\"file_name\"], photo_df[\"fold\"])\n)\n\nid_to_file = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img[\"file_name\"]\n    for img in images_list\n}\n\nbatch_df[\"fold\"] = batch_df[\"file_name\"].map(\n    file_to_fold\n)\n\nassert batch_df[\"fold\"].notna().all()\n\n# Each physical image's annotation batches must share one fold.\nassert (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"fold\"].nunique() == 1\n).all()\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Propagate folds to individual filament annotations\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndf_eda = df_eda.drop(\n    columns=[\"fold\"],\n    errors=\"ignore\"\n).copy()\n\ndf_eda[\"file_name\"] = df_eda[\"image_id\"].map(id_to_file)\n\nassert df_eda[\"file_name\"].notna().all()\n\ndf_eda[\"fold\"] = df_eda[\"file_name\"].map(file_to_fold)\n\nassert df_eda[\"fold\"].notna().all()\n\nassert (\n    df_eda.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"fold\"].nunique() == 1\n).all()\n\nassert df_eda[\"ann_id\"].nunique() == len(annotations_list)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7. Fold distribution and balance\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfold_summary = (\n    photo_df.groupby(\"fold\")\n    .agg(\n        physical_photos=(\"file_name\", \"nunique\"),\n        annotation_batches=(\"n_batches\", \"sum\"),\n        median_instances=(\"median_instances\", \"mean\")\n    )\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Physical Photo Distribution ---\")\ndisplay(fold_summary)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Observatory Distribution ---\")\ndisplay(\n    pd.crosstab(\n        photo_df[\"fold\"],\n        photo_df[\"site_code\"]\n    )\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Instance-count Quartile Distribution ---\")\ndisplay(\n    pd.crosstab(\n        photo_df[\"fold\"],\n        photo_df[\"count_bin\"]\n    )\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Annotation Counts ---\")\ndisplay(\n    df_eda.groupby(\"fold\")\n    .agg(\n        physical_photos=(\"file_name\", \"nunique\"),\n        filaments=(\"ann_id\", \"nunique\")\n    )\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Final leakage assertions\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nassert photo_df[\"file_name\"].nunique() == 707\nassert batch_df[\"image_id\"].nunique() == 1154\nassert df_eda[\"ann_id\"].nunique() == 8199\n\n# Every unique photo appears in exactly one fold.\nassert photo_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"fold\"].nunique().max() == 1\n\n# Every annotated batch inherits its physical photo's fold.\nassert all(\n    batch_df[\"fold\"] == batch_df[\"file_name\"].map(file_to_fold)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 9. Save reproducible manifests\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nphoto_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"folds_photo_level.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nbatch_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"folds_batch_level.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\ndf_eda[\n    [\"ann_id\", \"image_id\", \"file_name\", \"fold\"]\n].to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"folds_annotation_level.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"PHOTO-LEVEL FIVE-FOLD SPLIT: PASSED\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"Physical photographs:\", photo_df[\"file_name\"].nunique())\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", batch_df[\"image_id\"].nunique())\nprint(\"Filament instances:\", df_eda[\"ann_id\"].nunique())\nprint(\"Number of folds:\", photo_df[\"fold\"].nunique())\n\nprint(\"Saved all three fold manifests.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Training tile census\n\nThe next experiment answers:\n\n- How many positive and background tiles exist?\n- How many positive tiles contain only 1–10 foreground pixels?\n- How does this distribution change between folds?\n- How much does annotation-set selection change the number of positive tiles per photograph?\n- What background sampling ratio is justified?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 3B: TRAINING TILE CENSUS\n# No model training yet.\n# ============================================================\n\nimport gc\nimport cv2\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nTILE_SIZE = 512\nTILE_STRIDE = 384\n\nVALIDATION_FOLD = 0\nTRAIN_FOLDS = {1, 2, 3, 4}\n\nWORK_DIR = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    if Path(\"/kaggle/working\").exists()\n    else Path.cwd()\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Establish authoritative mappings\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img for img in images_list\n}\n\nbatch_ids_by_photo = (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"image_id\"]\n    .apply(list)\n    .to_dict()\n)\n\nphoto_fold_map = dict(\n    zip(photo_df[\"file_name\"], photo_df[\"fold\"])\n)\n\nassert len(photo_fold_map) == 707\nassert len(batch_df) == 1154\n\ntile_records = []\nbatch_records = []\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Process each physical photo once\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfor photo_idx, photo_row in photo_df.iterrows():\n\n    file_name = photo_row[\"file_name\"]\n    fold = int(photo_row[\"fold\"])\n\n    img_path = TRAIN_IMG_DIR / file_name\n\n    image = cv2.imread(\n        str(img_path),\n        cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n    )\n\n    if image is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot read image: {img_path}\")\n\n    batch_ids = sorted(\n        batch_ids_by_photo[file_name]\n    )\n\n    for batch_id in batch_ids:\n\n        info = image_info_by_id[batch_id]\n\n        height = int(info[\"height\"])\n        width = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n        if image.shape != (height, width):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Image shape mismatch: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        annotations = image_id_to_anns.get(\n            batch_id, []\n        )\n\n        # Construct semantic union directly.\n        # Avoid storing 26 full-sized instance masks.\n        semantic_mask = np.zeros(\n            (height, width),\n            dtype=np.uint8\n        )\n\n        for ann in annotations:\n\n            instance_mask = polygon_to_mask(\n                ann[\"segmentation\"],\n                height,\n                width\n            )\n\n            semantic_mask |= instance_mask\n\n        # Use the existing tile extraction implementation.\n        tiles = extract_tiles(\n            image,\n            semantic_mask,\n            spine_mask=None,\n            tile_size=TILE_SIZE,\n            stride=TILE_STRIDE,\n            min_filament_pixels=0\n        )\n\n        if not tiles:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"No tiles produced: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        positive_count = 0\n        negative_count = 0\n\n        batch_tile_indices = []\n\n        for tile_idx, tile in enumerate(tiles):\n\n            pixel_count = int(tile[\"pixel_count\"])\n\n            is_positive = pixel_count > 0\n\n            if is_positive:\n                positive_count += 1\n            else:\n                negative_count += 1\n\n            y, x, h, w = tile[\"coords\"]\n\n            batch_tile_indices.append(tile_idx)\n\n            tile_records.append({\n\n                \"file_name\": file_name,\n                \"image_id\": batch_id,\n                \"fold\": fold,\n\n                \"split\": (\n                    \"validation\"\n                    if fold == VALIDATION_FOLD\n                    else \"train\"\n                ),\n\n                \"tile_idx\": tile_idx,\n\n                \"y\": y,\n                \"x\": x,\n                \"height\": h,\n                \"width\": w,\n\n                \"positive_pixels\": pixel_count,\n                \"is_positive\": is_positive\n\n            })\n\n        if positive_count + negative_count != len(tiles):\n            raise AssertionError(\"Tile accounting mismatch.\")\n\n        batch_records.append({\n\n            \"file_name\": file_name,\n            \"image_id\": batch_id,\n            \"fold\": fold,\n\n            \"n_instances\": len(annotations),\n\n            \"total_tiles\": len(tiles),\n\n            \"positive_tiles\": positive_count,\n            \"negative_tiles\": negative_count,\n\n            \"foreground_pixels\": int(semantic_mask.sum()),\n\n            \"positive_tile_fraction\": (\n                positive_count / len(tiles)\n            ),\n\n            \"empty_annotation_set\": len(annotations) == 0\n\n        })\n\n    if (photo_idx + 1) % 100 == 0:\n        print(\n            f\"Processed {photo_idx + 1}/\"\n            f\"{len(photo_df)} physical photographs\"\n        )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Construct tile manifests\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntile_manifest_df = pd.DataFrame(tile_records)\nbatch_tile_summary = pd.DataFrame(batch_records)\n\nassert len(batch_tile_summary) == 1154\n\nassert len(tile_manifest_df) == (\n    1154 * 25\n)\n\nassert (\n    batch_tile_summary[\"positive_tiles\"]\n    + batch_tile_summary[\"negative_tiles\"]\n    == batch_tile_summary[\"total_tiles\"]\n).all()\n\nassert (\n    batch_tile_summary[\"total_tiles\"] == 25\n).all()\n\nassert not tile_manifest_df.duplicated(\n    [\"image_id\", \"tile_idx\"]\n).any()\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Aggregate annotation batches at physical-photo level\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Uniform random selection of annotation batches means\n# the expected tile statistics per physical photo are\n# the mean over its annotation batches.\n\nphoto_tile_summary = (\n\n    batch_tile_summary.groupby(\"file_name\")\n\n    .agg(\n\n        fold=(\"fold\", \"first\"),\n\n        n_batches=(\"image_id\", \"nunique\"),\n\n        expected_positive_tiles=(\n            \"positive_tiles\", \"mean\"\n        ),\n\n        expected_negative_tiles=(\n            \"negative_tiles\", \"mean\"\n        ),\n\n        min_positive_tiles=(\n            \"positive_tiles\", \"min\"\n        ),\n\n        max_positive_tiles=(\n            \"positive_tiles\", \"max\"\n        ),\n\n        mean_foreground_pixels=(\n            \"foreground_pixels\", \"mean\"\n        )\n\n    )\n\n    .reset_index()\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Training / validation distribution\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"TILE CENSUS\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Total annotation-set tile candidates:\", len(tile_manifest_df))\nprint(\"Unique physical photographs:\", len(photo_tile_summary))\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Physical-photo-level tile statistics ---\")\n\nphoto_tile_summary[\"positive_tile_range\"] = (\n    photo_tile_summary[\"max_positive_tiles\"]\n    - photo_tile_summary[\"min_positive_tiles\"]\n)\n\ndisplay(\n    photo_tile_summary.groupby(\"fold\").agg(\n        physical_photos=(\"file_name\", \"nunique\"),\n        mean_positive_tiles=(\"expected_positive_tiles\", \"mean\"),\n        mean_negative_tiles=(\"expected_negative_tiles\", \"mean\"),\n        mean_positive_tile_range=(\"positive_tile_range\", \"mean\")\n    ).round(3)\n)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Candidate tiles in each split\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Candidate tile distribution ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    tile_manifest_df.groupby(\"split\").agg(\n\n        total_tile_candidates=(\"tile_idx\", \"size\"),\n\n        positive_tile_candidates=(\"is_positive\", \"sum\"),\n\n        negative_tile_candidates=(\n            \"is_positive\",\n            lambda x: int((~x).sum())\n        ),\n\n        unique_photos=(\"file_name\", \"nunique\")\n\n    )\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7. Foreground pixel distribution in positive tiles\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\npositive_tile_df = tile_manifest_df[\n    tile_manifest_df[\"is_positive\"]\n].copy()\n\nbins = [0, 1, 10, 100, 1000, np.inf]\n\nlabels = [\n    \"1 pixel\",\n    \"2–10 pixels\",\n    \"11–100 pixels\",\n    \"101–1000 pixels\",\n    \">1000 pixels\"\n]\n\npositive_tile_df[\"foreground_bin\"] = pd.cut(\n    positive_tile_df[\"positive_pixels\"],\n    bins=bins,\n    labels=labels,\n    include_lowest=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Positive tile foreground distribution ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    pd.crosstab(\n        positive_tile_df[\"split\"],\n        positive_tile_df[\"foreground_bin\"],\n        normalize=\"index\"\n    ).mul(100).round(2)\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Foreground pixels per positive tile ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    positive_tile_df[\"positive_pixels\"].describe(\n        percentiles=[0.01, 0.05, 0.10, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.90, 0.95]\n    ).round(2)\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8. Annotation-set variation\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nmulti_batch_photo_stats = photo_tile_summary[\n    photo_tile_summary[\"n_batches\"] > 1\n].copy()\n\nmulti_batch_photo_stats[\"positive_tile_range\"] = (\n    multi_batch_photo_stats[\"max_positive_tiles\"]\n    - multi_batch_photo_stats[\"min_positive_tiles\"]\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Annotation-set variation in positive tile counts ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    multi_batch_photo_stats[\n        \"positive_tile_range\"\n    ].describe().round(3)\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 9. Save all manifests\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntile_manifest_df.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"tile_manifest_all_batches.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nbatch_tile_summary.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"batch_tile_summary.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nphoto_tile_summary.to_csv(\n    WORK_DIR / \"photo_tile_summary.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSaved:\")\nprint(\"tile_manifest_all_batches.csv\")\nprint(\"batch_tile_summary.csv\")\nprint(\"photo_tile_summary.csv\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 10. Zero-agreement visual verification\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# The two exceptional images should be visually inspected\n# before finalizing our annotation sampling strategy.\n\nzero_cases = pair_agreement_df[\n    pair_agreement_df[\"semantic_dice\"] <= 1e-12\n]\n\nif len(zero_cases) > 0:\n\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n        len(zero_cases),\n        4,\n        figsize=(18, 4.5 * len(zero_cases)),\n        squeeze=False\n    )\n\n    for row_idx, (_, record) in enumerate(\n        zero_cases.iterrows()\n    ):\n\n        filename = record[\"file_name\"]\n\n        image = cv2.imread(\n            str(TRAIN_IMG_DIR / filename),\n            cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n        )\n\n        target_a = build_batch_targets(record[\"batch_A\"])\n        target_b = build_batch_targets(record[\"batch_B\"])\n\n        mask_a = mask_utils.decode(\n            target_a[\"semantic_rle\"]\n        ).astype(bool)\n\n        mask_b = mask_utils.decode(\n            target_b[\"semantic_rle\"]\n        ).astype(bool)\n\n        overlap = mask_a & mask_b\n\n        rgb = cv2.cvtColor(\n            image,\n            cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB\n        )\n\n        overlay = rgb.copy()\n\n        overlay[mask_a & ~mask_b] = (255, 60, 60)\n        overlay[mask_b & ~mask_a] = (50, 220, 255)\n        overlay[overlap] = (255, 225, 0)\n\n        axes[row_idx, 0].imshow(image, cmap=\"gray\")\n        axes[row_idx, 0].set_title(filename)\n\n        axes[row_idx, 1].imshow(mask_a, cmap=\"gray\")\n        axes[row_idx, 1].set_title(\n            f\"Batch A: {record['batch_A']}\"\n        )\n\n        axes[row_idx, 2].imshow(mask_b, cmap=\"gray\")\n        axes[row_idx, 2].set_title(\n            f\"Batch B: {record['batch_B']}\"\n        )\n\n        axes[row_idx, 3].imshow(overlay)\n        axes[row_idx, 3].set_title(\n            \"Red: A only | Cyan: B only | Yellow: overlap\"\n        )\n\n        for ax in axes[row_idx]:\n            ax.axis(\"off\")\n\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\nprint(\"\\nSTAGE 3B TILE CENSUS COMPLETED.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Training Data Engineering\n\nBefore creating a U-Net, we need a reproducible training dataset.\nOur first model experiment: A0\nBaseline architecture\n\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\">\n\n<img src=\"attachment:6f6c1155-a2b1-464b-add1-f10152d5353d.png\" width=\"420\">\n\n</td>\n\n<td width=\"50%\">\n\n| Component | Initial Choice |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| Input | 1-channel grayscale image |\n| Input resolution | 512 × 512 |\n| Model | U-Net |\n| Encoder | ResNet34, ImageNet initialization |\n| Output | One foreground logit channel |\n| Loss | BCE + soft Dice |\n| Optimizer | AdamW |\n| Validation | Full 2048 × 2048 images |\n| Primary metrics | Dice, IoU, PQ |\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>","metadata":{},"attachments":{"6f6c1155-a2b1-464b-add1-f10152d5353d.png":{"image/png":""},"0c5e0afa-b481-415b-a069-eed9a16b1e10.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Now we convert the validated data into something the neural network can actually consume.\n1. Architecture of the data pipeline\n   \nWe propose a photo-centric Dataset, rather than a conventional tile-centric Dataset.\n\nWhy?\n\nA physical photograph has 25 tiles, but it may have multiple annotation sets. We want to select one annotation set for the entire photograph in each epoch.\n\nOur Dataset will therefore return:\nOne Dataset sample = one physical photograph\n\n**Image tiles (25) - 512 × 512 grayscale patches | Target tiles (25) - Corresponding binary masks**\n\n\nOne randomly selected annotation batch supplies all 25 masks. The original photograph is read only once per Dataset sample.\n\nThis avoids repeatedly loading the same JPEG 25 times and prevents different tiles from the same photograph receiving inconsistent annotator labels.\n\nWe will calculate grayscale mean and standard deviation using only the 565 training photographs.\n\nWe will not use validation images to estimate normalization parameters.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# STAGE 3C: FOLD PARTITIONS + VERIFIED NORMALIZATION\n# ============================================================\n\ntrain_photo_df = (\n    photo_df[\n        photo_df[\"fold\"].isin([1, 2, 3, 4])\n    ]\n    .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nval_photo_df = (\n    photo_df[\n        photo_df[\"fold\"] == 0\n    ]\n    .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nassert len(train_photo_df) == 565\nassert len(val_photo_df) == 142\n\nassert set(train_photo_df[\"file_name\"]).isdisjoint(\n    set(val_photo_df[\"file_name\"])\n)\n\nassert df_eda[\"ann_id\"].nunique() == 8199\n\n# Reuse the verified training-fold statistics.\n# Do not read all 565 photos again.\n\nnormalization_stats = {\n    \"mean\": 0.3265100952769327,\n    \"std\": 0.22311718458989044,\n    \"mean_raw\": 83.26007429561784,\n    \"std_raw\": 56.894882070422064,\n    \"num_images\": 565,\n    \"num_pixels\": 2369781760,\n    \"source\": \"A0 training-fold-only statistics\",\n    \"fold_seed\": 42,\n    \"training_folds\": [1, 2, 3, 4]\n}\n\nassert normalization_stats[\"std\"] > 0\n\nprint(\"Training physical photos:\", len(train_photo_df))\nprint(\"Validation physical photos:\", len(val_photo_df))\nprint(\"Training-fold mean:\", normalization_stats[\"mean\"])\nprint(\"Training-fold std:\", normalization_stats[\"std\"])\n\nprint(\"\\nFold partition and normalization: PASSED\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Implement full-image sliding-window inference\nFor neural-network probability maps, we also need a separate weighted reconstruction function. This uses the same tile coordinates during training and inference. Overlapping predictions are blended with positive weights so no image pixels are discarded.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4B: FULL-IMAGE PROBABILITY RECONSTRUCTION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nTILE_SIZE = 512\nTILE_STRIDE = 384\n\nTILE_MICRO_BATCH = 8\n\nMEAN = normalization_stats[\"mean\"]\nSTD = normalization_stats[\"std\"]\n\nAMP_ENABLED = torch.cuda.is_available()\n\n\ndef create_blend_window(tile_size=512, min_weight=0.05):\n    \"\"\"\n    Positive Hann-style window.\n\n    The floor prevents zero-weight pixels at tile boundaries.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    one_d = np.hanning(tile_size).astype(np.float32)\n\n    window = np.outer(one_d, one_d)\n\n    return np.maximum(\n        window,\n        min_weight\n    ).astype(np.float32)\n\n\nBLEND_WINDOW = create_blend_window(TILE_SIZE)\n\n\ndef predict_full_image_probability(\n    model,\n    image,\n    device,\n    micro_batch_size=TILE_MICRO_BATCH\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Predict one entire grayscale image using overlapping tiles.\n\n    Returns:\n        Full-resolution probability map of shape (2048, 2048).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if image.ndim != 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected grayscale image.\")\n\n    height, width = image.shape\n\n    if height != 2048 or width != 2048:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unexpected image dimensions.\")\n\n    if image.dtype != np.uint8:\n        raise TypeError(\"Expected uint8 image.\")\n\n    dummy_mask = np.zeros_like(image, dtype=np.uint8)\n\n    tiles = extract_tiles(\n        image,\n        dummy_mask,\n        spine_mask=None,\n        tile_size=TILE_SIZE,\n        stride=TILE_STRIDE,\n        min_filament_pixels=0\n    )\n\n    expected_tiles = 25\n\n    if len(tiles) != expected_tiles:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            f\"Expected {expected_tiles} tiles; got {len(tiles)}\"\n        )\n\n    tile_images = np.stack([\n        tile[\"img_tile\"] for tile in tiles\n    ])\n\n    probability_sum = np.zeros(\n        (height, width),\n        dtype=np.float32\n    )\n\n    weight_sum = np.zeros(\n        (height, width),\n        dtype=np.float32\n    )\n\n    was_training = model.training\n    model.eval()\n\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n\n        for start in range(\n            0,\n            len(tiles),\n            micro_batch_size\n        ):\n\n            end = min(\n                start + micro_batch_size,\n                len(tiles)\n            )\n\n            raw = torch.from_numpy(\n                tile_images[start:end, None].copy()\n            )\n\n            x = raw.to(\n                device,\n                dtype=torch.float32,\n                non_blocking=True\n            )\n\n            x = x / 255.0\n\n            x = (x - MEAN) / STD\n\n            with torch.autocast(\n                device_type=\"cuda\",\n                dtype=torch.float16,\n                enabled=AMP_ENABLED\n            ):\n\n                logits = model(x)\n\n            probabilities = torch.sigmoid(\n                logits.float()\n            ).cpu().numpy()[:, 0]\n\n            for local_idx, tile_idx in enumerate(\n                range(start, end)\n            ):\n\n                y, x0, h, w = tiles[tile_idx][\"coords\"]\n\n                pred_patch = probabilities[local_idx]\n\n                weight = BLEND_WINDOW[:h, :w]\n\n                probability_sum[\n                    y:y+h,\n                    x0:x0+w\n                ] += pred_patch * weight\n\n                weight_sum[\n                    y:y+h,\n                    x0:x0+w\n                ] += weight\n\n    if np.any(weight_sum <= 0):\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"Some full-image pixels were not covered.\"\n        )\n\n    reconstructed_probability = (\n        probability_sum / weight_sum\n    )\n\n    if was_training:\n        model.train()\n\n    if not np.isfinite(reconstructed_probability).all():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Invalid reconstructed probabilities.\")\n\n    return reconstructed_probability\n\n\nprint(\"Full-image inference utilities initialized.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Implement the Dataset classes\n\nWe will have two Dataset classes:\n- PhysicalPhotoTileDataset: training, one annotation set selected per photo per epoch.\n- ValidationPhotoDataset: full-resolution image and every available annotation set.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 3C: PYTORCH DATASET IMPLEMENTATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport torch\n\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Build independent annotation mappings.\n\nannotations_by_batch = defaultdict(list)\n\nfor ann in annotations_list:\n    annotations_by_batch[ann[\"image_id\"]].append(ann)\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img\n    for img in images_list\n}\n\nbatch_ids_by_photo = (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"image_id\"]\n    .apply(lambda x: sorted(x.tolist()))\n    .to_dict()\n)\n\n\ndef build_semantic_mask(batch_id):\n    \"\"\"\n    Produce the union of filament masks for one annotation batch.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    info = image_info_by_id[batch_id]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=np.uint8)\n\n    for ann in annotations_by_batch[batch_id]:\n\n        instance_mask = polygon_to_mask(\n            ann[\"segmentation\"],\n            h,\n            w\n        )\n\n        mask |= instance_mask\n\n    return mask\n\n\nclass PhysicalPhotoTileDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"\n    Training Dataset.\n\n    One item represents one physical photograph and returns:\n        25 grayscale tiles\n        25 semantic-mask tiles\n\n    One annotation batch is sampled deterministically\n    for the photograph during each epoch.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        photo_records,\n        image_dir,\n        batch_ids_by_photo,\n        tile_size=512,\n        stride=384,\n        seed=42\n    ):\n\n        self.photos = (\n            photo_records.sort_values(\"file_name\")\n            .to_dict(\"records\")\n        )\n\n        self.image_dir = Path(image_dir)\n\n        self.batch_ids_by_photo = batch_ids_by_photo\n\n        self.tile_size = tile_size\n        self.stride = stride\n        self.seed = seed\n\n        self.epoch = 0\n\n        for photo in self.photos:\n\n            if photo[\"file_name\"] not in self.batch_ids_by_photo:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"No annotation batch: {photo['file_name']}\"\n                )\n\n    def set_epoch(self, epoch):\n\n        self.epoch = int(epoch)\n\n    def __len__(self):\n\n        return len(self.photos)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, index):\n\n        photo = self.photos[index]\n\n        file_name = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 1. Deterministic annotation-set selection\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        available_batches = self.batch_ids_by_photo[\n            file_name\n        ]\n\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(\n            np.random.SeedSequence([\n                self.seed,\n                self.epoch,\n                index\n            ])\n        )\n\n        batch_position = int(\n            rng.integers(len(available_batches))\n        )\n\n        selected_batch = available_batches[\n            batch_position\n        ]\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 2. Load the physical image exactly once\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        image = cv2.imread(\n            str(self.image_dir / file_name),\n            cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n        )\n\n        if image is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Cannot read image: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        if image.shape != (2048, 2048):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Unexpected image dimensions: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 3. Generate semantic mask\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        mask = build_semantic_mask(\n            selected_batch\n        )\n\n        if mask.shape != image.shape:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Image/mask shape mismatch: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 4. Extract all tiles\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        tiles = extract_tiles(\n            image,\n            mask,\n            spine_mask=None,\n            tile_size=self.tile_size,\n            stride=self.stride,\n            min_filament_pixels=0\n        )\n\n        if len(tiles) != 25:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Expected 25 tiles, found {len(tiles)}\"\n            )\n\n        image_tiles = np.stack([\n            tile[\"img_tile\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ])\n\n        mask_tiles = np.stack([\n            tile[\"mask_tile\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ])\n\n        tile_pixel_counts = np.asarray([\n            tile[\"pixel_count\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ], dtype=np.int64)\n\n        tile_coords = np.asarray([\n            tile[\"coords\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ], dtype=np.int64)\n\n        # [25, 1, 512, 512]\n        image_tiles = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            image_tiles[:, None]\n        )\n\n        mask_tiles = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            mask_tiles[:, None]\n        )\n\n        return {\n\n            \"images\": torch.from_numpy(\n                image_tiles\n            ),\n\n            \"masks\": torch.from_numpy(\n                mask_tiles\n            ),\n\n            \"tile_pixel_counts\": torch.from_numpy(\n                tile_pixel_counts\n            ),\n\n            \"tile_coords\": torch.from_numpy(\n                tile_coords\n            ),\n\n            \"file_name\": file_name,\n\n            \"batch_id\": selected_batch,\n\n            \"fold\": int(photo[\"fold\"])\n        }\n\n\nclass ValidationPhotoDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validation Dataset.\n\n    One item represents one physical photograph.\n\n    Returns:\n        Full grayscale image.\n        One semantic mask per annotation batch.\n\n    No annotator sampling and no random augmentation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        photo_records,\n        image_dir,\n        batch_ids_by_photo\n    ):\n\n        self.photos = (\n            photo_records.sort_values(\"file_name\")\n            .to_dict(\"records\")\n        )\n\n        self.image_dir = Path(image_dir)\n\n        self.batch_ids_by_photo = batch_ids_by_photo\n\n    def __len__(self):\n\n        return len(self.photos)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, index):\n\n        photo = self.photos[index]\n\n        file_name = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\n        image = cv2.imread(\n            str(self.image_dir / file_name),\n            cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n        )\n\n        if image is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Cannot read image: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        if image.shape != (2048, 2048):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Unexpected dimensions: {file_name}\"\n            )\n\n        batch_ids = self.batch_ids_by_photo[\n            file_name\n        ]\n\n        semantic_masks = [\n            build_semantic_mask(batch_id)\n            for batch_id in batch_ids\n        ]\n\n        targets = np.stack(semantic_masks)\n\n        # [N_annotation_sets, 1, 2048, 2048]\n        targets = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            targets[:, None]\n        )\n\n        image = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            image[None]\n        )\n\n        return {\n\n            \"image\": torch.from_numpy(image),\n\n            \"target_masks\": torch.from_numpy(targets),\n\n            \"file_name\": file_name,\n\n            \"batch_ids\": batch_ids,\n\n            \"fold\": int(photo[\"fold\"])\n        }\n\n\nprint(\"Training photographs:\", len(train_photo_df))\nprint(\"Validation photographs:\", len(val_photo_df))\n\nprint(\"Training Dataset classes defined.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Build and test DataLoaders\n\nWe start with a small, conservative configuration. We do not set many workers or aggressive prefetching until we verify memory and Kaggle performance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 3C: DATALOADER CONSTRUCTION AND SMOKE TEST\n# ============================================================\n\nSEED = 42\n\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\n\ntrain_dataset = PhysicalPhotoTileDataset(\n    photo_records=train_photo_df,\n    image_dir=TRAIN_IMG_DIR,\n    batch_ids_by_photo=batch_ids_by_photo,\n    tile_size=512,\n    stride=384,\n    seed=SEED\n)\n\nval_dataset = ValidationPhotoDataset(\n    photo_records=val_photo_df,\n    image_dir=TRAIN_IMG_DIR,\n    batch_ids_by_photo=batch_ids_by_photo\n)\n\nloader_generator = torch.Generator()\nloader_generator.manual_seed(SEED)\n\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(\n    train_dataset,\n    batch_size=2,       # Two physical photos\n    shuffle=True,\n    num_workers=0,      # Initial debugging configuration\n    pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available(),\n    drop_last=False,\n    generator=loader_generator\n)\n\nval_loader = DataLoader(\n    val_dataset,\n    batch_size=1,\n    shuffle=False,\n    num_workers=0,\n    pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available()\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Training batch validation\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntrain_dataset.set_epoch(0)\n\ntrain_sample = next(iter(train_loader))\n\nx = train_sample[\"images\"]\ny = train_sample[\"masks\"]\n\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"TRAINING DATALOADER\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"Image shape:\", tuple(x.shape))\nprint(\"Mask shape:\", tuple(y.shape))\n\nprint(\"Image dtype:\", x.dtype)\nprint(\"Mask dtype:\", y.dtype)\n\nprint(\"Selected files:\", train_sample[\"file_name\"])\nprint(\"Selected annotation batches:\", train_sample[\"batch_id\"])\n\nprint(\n    \"Positive tiles per photo:\",\n    (train_sample[\"tile_pixel_counts\"] > 0).sum(dim=1)\n)\n\nassert x.shape == (2, 25, 1, 512, 512)\nassert y.shape == (2, 25, 1, 512, 512)\n\nassert x.dtype == torch.uint8\nassert y.dtype == torch.uint8\n\nassert set(torch.unique(y).tolist()).issubset({0, 1})\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Check epoch-wise annotator selection\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntrain_dataset.set_epoch(1)\n\nsample_epoch_1 = train_dataset[0]\n\ntrain_dataset.set_epoch(2)\n\nsample_epoch_2 = train_dataset[0]\n\nprint(\"\\nEpoch 1 selected annotation:\",\n      sample_epoch_1[\"batch_id\"])\n\nprint(\"Epoch 2 selected annotation:\",\n      sample_epoch_2[\"batch_id\"])\n\n# Different epochs may select the same annotation by chance.\n# Both selections must come from the valid annotation options.\n\nassert sample_epoch_1[\"batch_id\"] in (\n    batch_ids_by_photo[sample_epoch_1[\"file_name\"]]\n)\n\nassert sample_epoch_2[\"batch_id\"] in (\n    batch_ids_by_photo[sample_epoch_2[\"file_name\"]]\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Validation batch verification\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nval_sample = next(iter(val_loader))\n\nval_image = val_sample[\"image\"]\nval_targets = val_sample[\"target_masks\"]\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"VALIDATION DATALOADER\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"Image shape:\", tuple(val_image.shape))\nprint(\"Target masks shape:\", tuple(val_targets.shape))\n\nprint(\"Filename:\", val_sample[\"file_name\"])\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", val_sample[\"batch_ids\"])\n\nassert val_image.shape == (1, 1, 2048, 2048)\n\nassert val_targets.ndim == 5\n\nassert val_targets.shape[0] == 1\nassert val_targets.shape[2:] == (1, 2048, 2048)\n\nassert val_targets.dtype == torch.uint8\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Environment check\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"COMPUTE ENVIRONMENT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"PyTorch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"CUDA available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\n\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n\n    print(\"GPU:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n\n    print(\n        \"GPU memory:\",\n        round(\n            torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory\n            / 1024**3,\n            2\n        ),\n        \"GB\"\n    )\n\nelse:\n\n    print(\"Running on CPU\")\n\n\nprint(\"\\nDATASET AND DATALOADER SMOKE TEST: PASSED\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Define the augmentation policy\n\nFor A0, we will use modest transformations, not aggressive image manipulation.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# TRAINING AUGMENTATION AND NORMALIZATION\n# ============================================================\n\ndef augment_and_normalize(\n    images_uint8,\n    masks_uint8,\n    mean,\n    std,\n    training=True\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Input:\n        images_uint8: [B, 1, H, W]\n        masks_uint8:  [B, C, H, W]\n\n    C = 1 for A0.\n    C = 2 for A1:\n        channel 0 = semantic filament mask\n        channel 1 = auxiliary spine mask.\n\n    Every geometric transformation is synchronized across\n    the image and all target channels.\n    Photometric transformations affect only the image.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    images = images_uint8.float() / 255.0\n    masks = masks_uint8.float()\n\n    if training:\n\n        for i in range(images.shape[0]):\n\n            # Random rotation by 0, 90, 180 or 270 degrees\n            k = int(torch.randint(0, 4, ()).item())\n\n            images[i] = torch.rot90(\n                images[i], k, dims=(-2, -1)\n            )\n\n            masks[i] = torch.rot90(\n                masks[i], k, dims=(-2, -1)\n            )\n\n            # Horizontal reflection\n            if torch.rand(()) < 0.5:\n\n                images[i] = torch.flip(\n                    images[i], dims=(-1,)\n                )\n\n                masks[i] = torch.flip(\n                    masks[i], dims=(-1,)\n                )\n\n            # Vertical reflection\n            if torch.rand(()) < 0.5:\n\n                images[i] = torch.flip(\n                    images[i], dims=(-2,)\n                )\n\n                masks[i] = torch.flip(\n                    masks[i], dims=(-2,)\n                )\n\n            # Mild photometric perturbation\n            contrast = 0.9 + 0.2 * torch.rand(())\n\n            brightness = (\n                -0.03 + 0.06 * torch.rand(())\n            )\n\n            images[i] = torch.clamp(\n                images[i] * contrast + brightness,\n                0.0,\n                1.0\n            )\n\n    images = (\n        images - mean\n    ) / std\n\n    return images, masks","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"These geometric transformations are appropriate for our initial binary morphology task because we are not predicting chirality. Do not reuse them unchanged in a future chirality-classification experiment.\n\nWe are deliberately not applying CLAHE, synthetic filament insertion, aggressive blur or limb-darkening correction","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Build the A0 U-Net\n\nWe will use the architecture established in our research plan:\n\nU-Net + ResNet34 encoder + ImageNet initialization.\n\nThe Segmentation Models PyTorch library supports a one-channel ResNet34 U-Net directly. Its grayscale adaptation reuses the ImageNet first-convolution weights by summing the RGB filters.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"%pip install segmentation-models-pytorch -q","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Config","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4A: ARCHITECTURE DEPENDENCY CHECK\n# ============================================================\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport torch\n\nif importlib.util.find_spec(\n    \"segmentation_models_pytorch\"\n) is None:\n\n    raise ImportError(\n        \"SMP is not installed. Run this in a separate notebook cell:\\n\"\n        \"%pip install segmentation-models-pytorch==0.5.0\"\n    )\n\nimport segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n\nprint(\"PyTorch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"SMP:\", smp.__version__)\n\nassert torch.cuda.is_available()\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\")\n\nprint(\"GPU:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<div align=\"center\">\n    <img src=\"attachment:c0b18c21-af53-4b59-aa9b-fc0e6ba94677.png\" width=\"700\">\n</div>\n\nThe architecture has two major parts:\n\n- Encoder: ResNet34 extracts progressively more abstract image features at multiple resolutions.\n- Decoder: U-Net reconstructs the spatial detail using skip connections from the encoder.\nThe decoder is important because filament boundaries and fine structures need spatial information that may be lost in aggressive downsampling.","metadata":{},"attachments":{"c0b18c21-af53-4b59-aa9b-fc0e6ba94677.png":{"image/png":""},"eaecdea3-acce-400e-8fbb-b3901bfaedd0.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Model Architecture","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4A: A0 MODEL CONSTRUCTION\n# ============================================================\n\nmodel = smp.Unet(\n    encoder_name=\"resnet34\",\n    encoder_weights=\"imagenet\",\n    in_channels=1,\n    classes=1,\n    activation=None\n).to(device)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Model statistics\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntotal_params = sum(\n    p.numel() for p in model.parameters()\n)\n\ntrainable_params = sum(\n    p.numel()\n    for p in model.parameters()\n    if p.requires_grad\n)\n\nfirst_conv = model.encoder.conv1\n\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"A0: BASELINE U-NET\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\n\nprint(\"Architecture: U-Net\")\nprint(\"Encoder: ResNet34\")\nprint(\"Encoder initialization: ImageNet\")\nprint(\"Input channels:\", first_conv.in_channels)\nprint(\"Output classes:\", model.segmentation_head[0].out_channels)\n\nprint(\"Total parameters:\", f\"{total_params:,}\")\nprint(\"Trainable parameters:\", f\"{trainable_params:,}\")\n\nprint(\n    \"First convolution shape:\",\n    tuple(first_conv.weight.shape)\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Model size (FP32 parameters):\",\n    f\"{total_params * 4 / 1024**2:.2f} MB\"\n)\n\nassert first_conv.in_channels == 1\nassert model.segmentation_head[0].out_channels == 1\n\nprint(\"\\nA0 model constructed successfully.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Forward-pass and gradient smoke test\n\nThis is where we verify that the model actually works with your data.\n\nWe will deliberately test two tile types: one positive and one background-only tile. We calculate BCE and Dice in FP32 even though the forward pass uses mixed precision. This helps avoid numerical instability in overlap calculations.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4A: FORWARD + BACKWARD SMOKE TEST\n# ============================================================\n\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Flatten photo batches into tile batches\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Previous DataLoader shape:\n# [2, 25, 1, 512, 512]\n\nflat_images = train_sample[\"images\"].reshape(\n    -1, 1, 512, 512\n)\n\nflat_masks = train_sample[\"masks\"].reshape(\n    -1, 1, 512, 512\n)\n\ntile_counts = flat_masks.sum(\n    dim=(1, 2, 3)\n)\n\npositive_indices = torch.where(\n    tile_counts > 0\n)[0]\n\nnegative_indices = torch.where(\n    tile_counts == 0\n)[0]\n\nif len(positive_indices) == 0 or len(negative_indices) == 0:\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        \"Smoke test requires positive and negative tiles.\"\n    )\n\nselected_indices = torch.stack([\n    positive_indices[0],\n    negative_indices[0]\n])\n\nx_raw = flat_images[selected_indices]\ny_raw = flat_masks[selected_indices]\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Apply the previously calculated training normalization\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nx_test, y_test = augment_and_normalize(\n    x_raw,\n    y_raw,\n    mean=normalization_stats[\"mean\"],\n    std=normalization_stats[\"std\"],\n    training=False\n)\n\nx_test = x_test.to(\n    device,\n    non_blocking=True\n)\n\ny_test = y_test.to(\n    device,\n    non_blocking=True\n)\n\nprint(\"Input:\", tuple(x_test.shape))\nprint(\"Target:\", tuple(y_test.shape))\n\nprint(\n    \"Target foreground pixels:\",\n    y_test.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3)).tolist()\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Forward pass\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nmodel.eval()\n\nif device.type == \"cuda\":\n    torch.cuda.reset_peak_memory_stats()\n\nwith torch.enable_grad():\n\n    with torch.autocast(\n        device_type=\"cuda\",\n        dtype=torch.float16,\n        enabled=True\n    ):\n\n        logits = model(x_test)\n\n    print(\"\\nLogit shape:\", tuple(logits.shape))\n    print(\"Logit dtype:\", logits.dtype)\n\n    assert logits.shape == y_test.shape\n    assert torch.isfinite(logits).all()\n\n    probabilities = torch.sigmoid(logits.float())\n\n    print(\n        \"Probability range:\",\n        probabilities.min().item(),\n        probabilities.max().item()\n    )\n\n    assert probabilities.min() >= 0\n    assert probabilities.max() <= 1\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Test the A0 loss calculation\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntargets = y_test.float()\nlogits_fp32 = logits.float()\n\nbce_loss = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(\n    logits_fp32,\n    targets\n)\n\nprobs = torch.sigmoid(logits_fp32)\n\nintersection = (\n    probs * targets\n).sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n\ndenominator = (\n    probs.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n    + targets.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n)\n\ndice_per_tile = (\n    2.0 * intersection + 1.0\n) / (\n    denominator + 1.0\n)\n\ndice_loss = (\n    1.0 - dice_per_tile\n).mean()\n\ntotal_loss = bce_loss + dice_loss\n\nprint(\"\\nBCE loss:\", bce_loss.item())\nprint(\"Dice loss:\", dice_loss.item())\nprint(\"Total loss:\", total_loss.item())\n\nassert torch.isfinite(total_loss)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Verify gradient flow without changing model weights\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\noptimizer_test = torch.optim.AdamW(\n    model.parameters(),\n    lr=3e-4,\n    weight_decay=1e-4\n)\n\nscaler_test = torch.amp.GradScaler(\n    \"cuda\",\n    enabled=True\n)\n\noptimizer_test.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n\nscaler_test.scale(total_loss).backward()\n\nscaler_test.unscale_(optimizer_test)\n\nfirst_conv_grad = model.encoder.conv1.weight.grad\n\nassert first_conv_grad is not None\nassert torch.isfinite(first_conv_grad).all()\n\ngrad_norm = torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n    first_conv_grad\n).item()\n\nprint(\"\\nFirst convolution gradient norm:\", grad_norm)\n\nassert grad_norm > 0\n\n# No optimizer step: this is strictly a smoke test.\noptimizer_test.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n\nprint(\"\\nForward pass: PASSED\")\nprint(\"Loss calculation: PASSED\")\nprint(\"Backward pass: PASSED\")\nprint(\"Model weights remain unmodified.\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. GPU memory\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n\n    allocated = (\n        torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated(device) / 1024**3\n    )\n\n    reserved = (\n        torch.cuda.max_memory_reserved(device) / 1024**3\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nPeak allocated GPU memory:\", round(allocated, 3), \"GB\")\n    print(\"Peak reserved GPU memory:\", round(reserved, 3), \"GB\")\n\n\ndel logits, probabilities, x_test, y_test\noptimizer_test.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n\ntorch.cuda.empty_cache()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Verify genuine multi-annotator sampling\n\nThis verifies that the random selection is reproducible and that all available annotation sets can be sampled. It does not require every epoch to select a different annotator.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# MULTI-ANNOTATOR SELECTION VALIDATION\n# ============================================================\n\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nmulti_indices = [\n    idx\n    for idx, photo in enumerate(train_dataset.photos)\n    if len(\n        train_dataset.batch_ids_by_photo[\n            photo[\"file_name\"]\n        ]\n    ) > 1\n]\n\nif not multi_indices:\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        \"No multi-annotator training photographs found.\"\n    )\n\ntest_idx = multi_indices[0]\n\nphoto = train_dataset.photos[test_idx]\nfile_name = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\navailable = train_dataset.batch_ids_by_photo[\n    file_name\n]\n\nselected_batches = []\n\nfor epoch in range(200):\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(\n        np.random.SeedSequence([\n            train_dataset.seed,\n            epoch,\n            test_idx\n        ])\n    )\n\n    selected_position = int(\n        rng.integers(len(available))\n    )\n\n    selected_batches.append(\n        available[selected_position]\n    )\n\nselection_counts = Counter(selected_batches)\n\nprint(\"Test photograph:\", file_name)\nprint(\"Available batches:\", available)\nprint(\"Selection frequencies over 200 epochs:\")\n\nfor batch_id, count in selection_counts.items():\n    print(batch_id, \":\", count)\n\nassert set(selection_counts.keys()) == set(available)\n\nprint(\"\\nMulti-annotator sampling test: PASSED\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Build the validation evaluator\n\nFor the initial A0 experiment, we will report:\n- Semantic Dice.\n- Semantic IoU.\n- Mean metrics per physical photograph.\n- Metrics separately against all annotation batches.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4B: FULL-IMAGE VALIDATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef calculate_binary_metrics(prediction, target):\n\n    prediction = np.asarray(\n        prediction, dtype=bool\n    )\n\n    target = np.asarray(\n        target, dtype=bool\n    )\n\n    intersection = np.logical_and(\n        prediction,\n        target\n    ).sum()\n\n    pred_area = prediction.sum()\n    target_area = target.sum()\n\n    union = np.logical_or(\n        prediction,\n        target\n    ).sum()\n\n    if pred_area + target_area == 0:\n        dice = 1.0\n    else:\n        dice = (\n            2.0 * intersection\n            / (pred_area + target_area)\n        )\n\n    iou = (\n        intersection / union\n        if union > 0 else 1.0\n    )\n\n    return float(dice), float(iou)\n\n\ndef validate_a0(\n    model,\n    val_loader,\n    device,\n    threshold=0.5\n):\n\n    batch_results = []\n    photo_results = []\n\n    model.eval()\n\n    for batch_idx, batch in enumerate(val_loader):\n\n        file_name = batch[\"file_name\"][0]\n\n        # [2048, 2048]\n        image = (\n            batch[\"image\"][0, 0]\n            .numpy()\n        )\n\n        # [N_annotation_sets, 2048, 2048]\n        targets = (\n            batch[\"target_masks\"][0, :, 0]\n            .numpy()\n        )\n\n        batch_ids = batch[\"batch_ids\"]\n\n        probability_map = predict_full_image_probability(\n            model,\n            image,\n            device\n        )\n\n        prediction = probability_map >= threshold\n\n        photo_dices = []\n        photo_ious = []\n\n        for annotator_idx, target in enumerate(targets):\n\n            target_mask = target > 0\n\n            dice, iou = calculate_binary_metrics(\n                prediction,\n                target_mask\n            )\n\n            photo_dices.append(dice)\n            photo_ious.append(iou)\n\n            # DataLoader collates annotation IDs into tuples.\n            batch_id = (\n                batch_ids[annotator_idx][0]\n                if isinstance(batch_ids[annotator_idx], (list, tuple))\n                else batch_ids[annotator_idx]\n            )\n\n            batch_results.append({\n\n                \"file_name\": file_name,\n\n                \"image_id\": batch_id,\n\n                \"dice\": dice,\n\n                \"iou\": iou,\n\n                \"prediction_pixels\": int(\n                    prediction.sum()\n                ),\n\n                \"target_pixels\": int(\n                    target_mask.sum()\n                ),\n\n                \"threshold\": threshold\n\n            })\n\n        # Equal weighting within each physical photograph\n        photo_results.append({\n\n            \"file_name\": file_name,\n\n            \"n_annotation_sets\": len(targets),\n\n            \"mean_batch_dice\": float(\n                np.mean(photo_dices)\n            ),\n\n            \"mean_batch_iou\": float(\n                np.mean(photo_ious)\n            )\n\n        })\n\n        if (batch_idx + 1) % 25 == 0:\n\n            print(\n                f\"Validated {batch_idx + 1}/\"\n                f\"{len(val_loader)} photographs\"\n            )\n\n    batch_df_result = pd.DataFrame(batch_results)\n\n    photo_df_result = pd.DataFrame(photo_results)\n\n    summary = {\n\n        \"mean_photo_dice\": float(\n            photo_df_result[\"mean_batch_dice\"].mean()\n        ),\n\n        \"mean_photo_iou\": float(\n            photo_df_result[\"mean_batch_iou\"].mean()\n        ),\n\n        \"mean_batch_dice\": float(\n            batch_df_result[\"dice\"].mean()\n        ),\n\n        \"mean_batch_iou\": float(\n            batch_df_result[\"iou\"].mean()\n        ),\n\n        \"n_photos\": len(photo_df_result),\n\n        \"n_annotation_sets\": len(batch_df_result)\n\n    }\n\n    return summary, photo_df_result, batch_df_result\n\n\nprint(\"Validation evaluator initialized.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Define the A0 loss\n\nWe will calculate BCE and Dice separately for each micro-batch.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4B: A0 BCE + SOFT DICE LOSS\n# ============================================================\n\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n\ndef a0_loss_function(logits, targets, smooth=1.0):\n\n    logits = logits.float()\n    targets = targets.float()\n\n    # Pixel-wise BCE\n    bce = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(\n        logits,\n        targets\n    )\n\n    probabilities = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n\n    # Dice calculated independently for every tile\n    intersection = (\n        probabilities * targets\n    ).sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n\n    denominator = (\n        probabilities.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n        + targets.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n    )\n\n    dice_per_tile = (\n        2.0 * intersection + smooth\n    ) / (\n        denominator + smooth\n    )\n\n    dice_loss = (\n        1.0 - dice_per_tile\n    ).mean()\n\n    total_loss = bce + dice_loss\n\n    return total_loss, bce.detach(), dice_loss.detach()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Implement the training engine\nThis is the main experiment code.\n\nIt implements:\n- One annotation set per physical photo per epoch.\n- All 25 tiles per selected photograph.\n- Eight-tile GPU micro-batches.\n- Correct gradient accumulation.\n- FP16 mixed precision.\n- AdamW.\n- Gradient clipping.\n- Full-image validation.\n- Best and last checkpoints.\n- Learning-rate scheduling.\n- Resume capability.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# STAGE 4B: A0 TRAINING ENGINE\n# ============================================================\n\nimport os\nimport random\nimport time\nimport json\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\n\nfrom torch.nn.utils import clip_grad_norm_\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Configuration\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nA0_CONFIG = {\n\n    \"model\": \"Unet\",\n\n    \"encoder\": \"resnet34\",\n\n    \"encoder_weights\": \"imagenet\",\n\n    \"input_channels\": 1,\n\n    \"output_channels\": 1,\n\n    \"tile_size\": 512,\n\n    \"stride\": 384,\n\n    \"photo_batch_size\": 2,\n\n    \"tile_micro_batch\": 8,\n\n    \"learning_rate\": 3e-4,\n\n    \"weight_decay\": 1e-4,\n\n    \"gradient_clip\": 1.0,\n\n    \"loss\": \"BCE + Soft Dice\",\n\n    \"amp\": True,\n\n    \"seed\": 42,\n\n    \"validation_fold\": 0\n\n}\n\nCHECKPOINT_DIR = WORK_DIR / \"a0_checkpoints\"\n\nCHECKPOINT_DIR.mkdir(\n    parents=True,\n    exist_ok=True\n)\n\nBEST_CHECKPOINT = (\n    CHECKPOINT_DIR / \"a0_best.pt\"\n)\n\nLAST_CHECKPOINT = (\n    CHECKPOINT_DIR / \"a0_last.pt\"\n)\n\nHISTORY_FILE = (\n    CHECKPOINT_DIR / \"a0_history.csv\"\n)\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\")\n\nassert device.type == \"cuda\"\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Deterministic setup\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef set_seed(seed):\n\n    random.seed(seed)\n\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Training and validation engine\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef train_a0(\n    model,\n    train_loader,\n    val_loader,\n    max_epochs=5,\n    resume=False\n):\n\n    set_seed(A0_CONFIG[\"seed\"])\n\n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(\n        model.parameters(),\n        lr=A0_CONFIG[\"learning_rate\"],\n        weight_decay=A0_CONFIG[\"weight_decay\"]\n    )\n\n    scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n        optimizer,\n        mode=\"max\",\n        factor=0.5,\n        patience=3,\n        min_lr=1e-6\n    )\n\n    scaler = torch.amp.GradScaler(\n        \"cuda\",\n        enabled=A0_CONFIG[\"amp\"]\n    )\n\n    start_epoch = 1\n\n    best_score = -np.inf\n\n    bad_epochs = 0\n\n    history = []\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n    # 4. Resume checkpoint if requested\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n\n    if resume:\n\n        if not LAST_CHECKPOINT.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(\n                \"No previous checkpoint available.\"\n            )\n\n        checkpoint = torch.load(\n            LAST_CHECKPOINT,\n            map_location=\"cpu\",\n            weights_only=False\n        )\n        \n        # Verify all saved RNG states have the required CPU format.\n        loader_state = checkpoint[\"loader_generator_state\"]\n        \n        print(\n            \"Loader RNG state:\",\n            type(loader_state),\n            loader_state.dtype,\n            loader_state.device,\n            loader_state.is_contiguous()\n        )\n        \n        assert loader_state.dtype == torch.uint8\n        assert loader_state.device.type == \"cpu\"\n        assert loader_state.is_contiguous()\n\n        model.load_state_dict(\n            checkpoint[\"model_state_dict\"]\n        )\n\n        optimizer.load_state_dict(\n            checkpoint[\"optimizer_state_dict\"]\n        )\n\n        scheduler.load_state_dict(\n            checkpoint[\"scheduler_state_dict\"]\n        )\n\n        scaler.load_state_dict(\n            checkpoint[\"scaler_state_dict\"]\n        )\n\n        start_epoch = checkpoint[\"epoch\"] + 1\n\n        best_score = checkpoint[\"best_score\"]\n\n        bad_epochs = checkpoint[\"bad_epochs\"]\n\n        history = checkpoint[\"history\"]\n\n        if (\n            checkpoint.get(\"loader_generator_state\")\n            is not None\n            and train_loader.generator is not None\n        ):\n\n            train_loader.generator.set_state(\n                checkpoint[\"loader_generator_state\"]\n            )\n\n        torch.set_rng_state(\n            checkpoint[\"torch_rng_state\"].cpu()\n        )\n\n        torch.cuda.set_rng_state_all(\n            checkpoint[\"cuda_rng_states\"]\n        )\n\n        print(\n            f\"Resuming from epoch {start_epoch}\"\n        )\n\n    else:\n\n        if LAST_CHECKPOINT.exists():\n            raise FileExistsError(\n                \"Previous checkpoint exists. \"\n                \"Set resume=True or move the old run.\"\n            )\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n    # 5. Epoch loop\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n\n    patience_early_stop = 7\n\n    micro_batch_size = A0_CONFIG[\"tile_micro_batch\"]\n\n    for epoch in range(start_epoch, max_epochs + 1):\n\n        epoch_start = time.time()\n\n        train_loader.dataset.set_epoch(epoch)\n\n        model.train()\n\n        total_loss_sum = 0.0\n        total_bce_sum = 0.0\n        total_dice_sum = 0.0\n\n        total_tile_count = 0\n\n        skipped_updates_epoch = 0\n        successful_updates_epoch = 0\n        consecutive_skips = 0\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n\n        print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\n        print(f\"A0 — EPOCH {epoch}/{max_epochs}\")\n        print(\"=\" * 65)\n\n        for step, batch in enumerate(train_loader):\n\n            # [B, 25, 1, 512, 512] -> [B*25, 1, 512, 512]\n            images = batch[\"images\"].reshape(\n                -1, 1, 512, 512\n            )\n\n            masks = batch[\"masks\"].reshape(\n                -1, 1, 512, 512\n            )\n\n            n_tiles = images.shape[0]\n\n            optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n\n            batch_loss_value = 0.0\n            batch_bce_value = 0.0\n            batch_dice_value = 0.0\n\n            # ------------------------------------------------\n            # Gradient accumulation over tile micro-batches\n            # ------------------------------------------------\n\n            for start in range(\n                0,\n                n_tiles,\n                micro_batch_size\n            ):\n\n                end = min(\n                    start + micro_batch_size,\n                    n_tiles\n                )\n\n                x_raw = images[start:end]\n\n                y_raw = masks[start:end]\n\n                x, y = augment_and_normalize(\n                    x_raw,\n                    y_raw,\n\n                    mean=normalization_stats[\"mean\"],\n\n                    std=normalization_stats[\"std\"],\n\n                    training=True\n                )\n\n                x = x.to(\n                    device,\n                    non_blocking=True\n                )\n\n                y = y.to(\n                    device,\n                    dtype=torch.float32,\n                    non_blocking=True\n                )\n\n                # Mixed-precision forward\n                \n                with torch.autocast(\n                    device_type=\"cuda\",\n                    dtype=torch.float16,\n                    enabled=A0_CONFIG[\"amp\"]\n                ):\n                \n                    logits = model(x)\n                \n                # Detect invalid forward activations before backward.\n                if not torch.isfinite(logits).all().item():\n                \n                    raise RuntimeError(\n                        f\"Non-finite logits. \"\n                        f\"Photos={batch['file_name']}, \"\n                        f\"Annotation sets={batch['batch_id']}, \"\n                        f\"Tiles={start}:{end}\"\n                    )\n                \n                micro_loss, bce, dice = a0_loss_function(\n                    logits, y\n                )\n                \n                if not torch.isfinite(micro_loss).item():\n                \n                    raise RuntimeError(\n                        f\"Non-finite loss. \"\n                        f\"Photos={batch['file_name']}, \"\n                        f\"Annotation sets={batch['batch_id']}, \"\n                        f\"Tiles={start}:{end}\"\n                    )\n\n\n                # Correctly weight each micro-batch by\n                # the number of tiles it contributes.\n                chunk_weight = (\n                    (end - start) / n_tiles\n                )\n\n                weighted_loss = (\n                    micro_loss * chunk_weight\n                )\n\n                scaler.scale(\n                    weighted_loss\n                ).backward()\n\n                batch_loss_value += (\n                    micro_loss.item() * chunk_weight\n                )\n\n                batch_bce_value += (\n                    bce.item() * chunk_weight\n                )\n\n                batch_dice_value += (\n                    dice.item() * chunk_weight\n                )\n\n                del x, y, logits, micro_loss\n            \n            # ------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Safe gradient validation and AMP recovery\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------\n            \n            # All micro-batch gradients have now been accumulated.\n            # Unscale exactly once before inspecting or clipping.\n            \n            scaler.unscale_(optimizer)\n            \n            bad_gradient_names = []\n            \n            for name, parameter in model.named_parameters():\n            \n                if parameter.grad is None:\n                    continue\n            \n                if not torch.isfinite(parameter.grad).all().item():\n            \n                    bad_gradient_names.append(name)\n            \n            \n            if bad_gradient_names:\n            \n                # GradScaler has recorded the non-finite gradients\n                # during unscale_. Its step() will skip the optimizer update.\n            \n                old_scale = scaler.get_scale()\n            \n                scaler.step(optimizer)\n            \n                scaler.update()\n            \n                new_scale = scaler.get_scale()\n            \n                optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n            \n                skipped_updates_epoch += 1\n                consecutive_skips += 1\n            \n                print(\"\\nWARNING: Non-finite gradients detected.\")\n            \n                print(\"Affected parameters:\", bad_gradient_names[:8])\n            \n                print(\"Affected parameter count:\", len(bad_gradient_names))\n            \n                print(\"Previous AMP scale:\", old_scale)\n            \n                print(\"Updated AMP scale:\", new_scale)\n            \n                print(\"Photos:\", batch[\"file_name\"])\n            \n                print(\"Annotation sets:\", batch[\"batch_id\"])\n            \n                if consecutive_skips >= 5:\n            \n                    raise RuntimeError(\n                        \"Five consecutive optimizer updates were skipped. \"\n                        \"Stop and investigate numerical instability.\"\n                    )\n            \n            else:\n            \n                # Safe to calculate and clip gradient norm.\n                grad_norm = clip_grad_norm_(\n                    model.parameters(),\n                    A0_CONFIG[\"gradient_clip\"]\n                )\n            \n                if not torch.isfinite(grad_norm).item():\n            \n                    raise RuntimeError(\n                        \"Gradient norm is non-finite although individual \"\n                        \"gradients passed the finite-value check. \"\n                        \"Investigate gradient norm overflow.\"\n                    )\n            \n                # Perform optimizer update and adjust scale.\n                scaler.step(optimizer)\n            \n                scaler.update()\n            \n                successful_updates_epoch += 1\n                consecutive_skips = 0\n            \n            \n            # ------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Accumulate loss statistics whether or not the update\n            # was skipped. These describe the forward-pass batches.\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------\n            \n            total_loss_sum += batch_loss_value * n_tiles\n            \n            total_bce_sum += batch_bce_value * n_tiles\n            \n            total_dice_sum += batch_dice_value * n_tiles\n            \n            total_tile_count += n_tiles\n\n\n            # Tile-weighted epoch statistics\n            total_loss_sum += batch_loss_value * n_tiles\n            total_bce_sum += batch_bce_value * n_tiles\n            total_dice_sum += batch_dice_value * n_tiles\n\n            total_tile_count += n_tiles\n\n            if (step + 1) % 50 == 0:\n\n                print(\n                    f\"Step {step+1}/{len(train_loader)} | \"\n                    f\"Loss={batch_loss_value:.4f}\"\n                )\n\n        train_loss = (\n            total_loss_sum / total_tile_count\n        )\n\n        train_bce = (\n            total_bce_sum / total_tile_count\n        )\n\n        train_dice = (\n            total_dice_sum / total_tile_count\n        )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 6. Full-resolution validation\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        val_summary, val_photo_df, val_batch_df = (\n            validate_a0(\n                model,\n                val_loader,\n                device,\n                threshold=0.5\n            )\n        )\n\n        validation_score = val_summary[\n            \"mean_photo_dice\"\n        ]\n\n        lr_used = optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"]\n\n        scheduler.step(validation_score)\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 7. Record results\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        elapsed = time.time() - epoch_start\n\n        record = {\n\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n\n            \"train_loss\": train_loss,\n\n            \"train_bce\": train_bce,\n\n            \"train_dice_loss\": train_dice,\n\n            \"val_photo_dice\": validation_score,\n\n            \"val_photo_iou\": val_summary[\"mean_photo_iou\"],\n\n            \"val_batch_dice\": val_summary[\"mean_batch_dice\"],\n\n            \"val_batch_iou\": val_summary[\"mean_batch_iou\"],\n\n            \"learning_rate\": lr_used,\n\n            \"elapsed_seconds\": elapsed,\n            \n            \"successful_updates\": successful_updates_epoch,\n\n            \"skipped_updates\": skipped_updates_epoch,\n            \n            \"amp_scale\": scaler.get_scale()\n\n        }\n\n        history.append(record)\n\n        val_photo_df.to_csv(\n            CHECKPOINT_DIR /\n            f\"validation_photos_epoch_{epoch:03d}.csv\",\n            index=False\n        )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 8. Best checkpoint\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        improved = (\n            validation_score > best_score\n        )\n\n        if improved:\n\n            best_score = validation_score\n\n            bad_epochs = 0\n\n            torch.save(\n                {\n                    \"epoch\": epoch,\n\n                    \"model_state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n\n                    \"best_val_dice\": best_score,\n\n                    \"normalization_stats\": normalization_stats,\n\n                    \"config\": A0_CONFIG\n                },\n                BEST_CHECKPOINT\n            )\n\n            print(\"Saved new BEST checkpoint.\")\n\n        else:\n\n            bad_epochs += 1\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 9. Resume checkpoint\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        loader_generator_state = (\n            train_loader.generator.get_state()\n            if train_loader.generator is not None\n            else None\n        )\n\n        last_state = {\n\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n\n            \"model_state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n\n            \"optimizer_state_dict\": optimizer.state_dict(),\n\n            \"scheduler_state_dict\": scheduler.state_dict(),\n\n            \"scaler_state_dict\": scaler.state_dict(),\n\n            \"best_score\": best_score,\n\n            \"bad_epochs\": bad_epochs,\n\n            \"history\": history,\n\n            \"loader_generator_state\": loader_generator_state,\n\n            \"torch_rng_state\": torch.get_rng_state(),\n\n            \"cuda_rng_states\": torch.cuda.get_rng_state_all()\n        }\n\n        torch.save(\n            last_state,\n            LAST_CHECKPOINT\n        )\n\n        pd.DataFrame(history).to_csv(\n            HISTORY_FILE,\n            index=False\n        )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 10. Epoch summary\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        print(\"\\nEPOCH SUMMARY\")\n\n        print(f\"Train loss: {train_loss:.5f}\")\n\n        print(f\"  BCE: {train_bce:.5f}\")\n\n        print(f\"  Dice loss: {train_dice:.5f}\")\n\n        print(\n            f\"Validation photo Dice: {validation_score:.5f}\"\n        )\n\n        print(\n            f\"Validation photo IoU: \"\n            f\"{val_summary['mean_photo_iou']:.5f}\"\n        )\n\n        print(f\"Learning rate: {lr_used:.7f}\")\n\n        print(f\"Best validation Dice: {best_score:.5f}\")\n\n        print(f\"Elapsed: {elapsed / 60:.2f} minutes\")\n\n        print(\n            \"Peak GPU memory:\",\n            round(\n                torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated() / 1024**3,\n                2\n            ),\n            \"GB\"\n        )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 11. Early stopping\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        if bad_epochs >= patience_early_stop:\n\n            print(\n                \"\\nEarly stopping triggered.\"\n            )\n\n            break\n\n    history_df = pd.DataFrame(history)\n\n    print(\"\\nA0 TRAINING RUN COMPLETED.\")\n\n    print(\"History:\", HISTORY_FILE)\n\n    print(\"Best checkpoint:\", BEST_CHECKPOINT)\n\n    print(\"Last checkpoint:\", LAST_CHECKPOINT)\n\n    return history_df\n\n\nprint(\"A0 training engine initialized.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Training pilot check on 3 epochs before final training on all 30 epochs ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# # ============================================================\n# # A0: INITIAL THREE-EPOCH PILOT\n# # ============================================================\n\n# history_df = train_a0(\n#     model=model,\n#     train_loader=train_loader,\n#     val_loader=val_loader,\n#     max_epochs=3,\n#     resume=False\n# )\n\n# display(history_df)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Checkoint inspection","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source