> 1:\n\n#         axes[row_idx, 4].imshow(\n#             target_masks[1],\n#             cmap=\"gray\"\n#         )\n#         axes[row_idx, 4].set_title(\n#             f\"Reference B: {batch_ids[1]}\"\n#         )\n\n#     else:\n\n#         axes[row_idx, 4].text(\n#             0.5, 0.5,\n#             \"Only one annotation set\",\n#             ha=\"center\",\n#             va=\"center\"\n#         )\n\n#     axes[row_idx, 5].imshow(overlay)\n#     axes[row_idx, 5].set_title(\n#         \"Red: FP | Cyan: FN | Yellow: overlap\"\n#     )\n\n#     for ax in axes[row_idx]:\n#         ax.axis(\"off\")\n\n# plt.tight_layout()\n# plt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# # ============================================================\n# # A0 CHECKPOINT HEALTH DIAGNOSTIC\n# # ============================================================\n\n# checkpoint = torch.load(\n#     LAST_CHECKPOINT,\n#     map_location=\"cpu\",\n#     weights_only=False\n# )\n\n# print(\"Saved epoch:\", checkpoint[\"epoch\"])\n# print(\"Saved best score:\", checkpoint[\"best_score\"])\n\n# print(\"\\nGradScaler state:\")\n\n# for key, value in checkpoint[\"scaler_state_dict\"].items():\n#     print(key, \":\", value)\n\n# bad_weights = []\n\n# for name, tensor in checkpoint[\"model_state_dict\"].items():\n\n#     if torch.is_floating_point(tensor):\n\n#         if not torch.isfinite(tensor).all():\n#             bad_weights.append(name)\n\n# print(\"\\nNon-finite model parameters:\", len(bad_weights))\n\n# if bad_weights:\n#     print(bad_weights[:10])\n\n# assert not bad_weights, \"Checkpoint contains invalid model weights.\"\n\n# print(\"\\nCheckpoint model weights: HEALTHY\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# history_df = train_a0(\n#     model=model,\n#     train_loader=train_loader,\n#     val_loader=val_loader,\n#     max_epochs=30,\n#     resume=True\n# )\n\n# display(history_df)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## A0 audit\n\nOur baseline was:\n\nA0 = ResNet34 Encoder + U-Net Decoder + BCE + Dice\n\nIts best checkpoint was epoch 23.\n\n| Measurement | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Best validation Dice | **0.6510** |\n| Best validation IoU | **0.5018** |\n| Final training loss | 0.2407 |\n| Final validation Dice | 0.6443 |\n| Total optimizer updates | 8,490 |\n| Skipped updates | 5 |\n\nThe network learned to distinguish filament-like structures from the solar background.\n\nThe fact that validation Dice improved from 0.5786 in epoch 1 to 0.6510 in epoch 23 confirms useful learning.\n\n**What needs improvement**\n\nFrom the qualitative results, we identified three important failure modes:\n\n1. Fragmentation: A single physical filament can produce several disconnected predicted regions.\n\n2. Incomplete structures: Thin structures and parts of elongated filaments are sometimes missed.\n\n3. Instance ambiguity: Semantic segmentation identifies foreground pixels but cannot reliably determine how many individual filaments are present.\n\nThese findings suggest that simply replacing ResNet34 with a larger backbone is not our first priority.\n\nWe should improve the supervision and instance reconstruction.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n---\n---\n---","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Final experiment directory\n\nThe new checkpoint policy\nEvery epoch must save:\n\nlast.pt — model, optimizer, scheduler, AMP scaler, epoch, history and RNG state.\n\nbest.pt — best model weights and associated evaluation metrics.\n\nhistory.csv — training and validation metrics.\n\nexperiment_metadata.json — architecture, normalization, seed, fold and software versions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## A1 Spine-Assisted Topology-Aware U-Net\n\nThe backbone remains ResNet34 + U-Net. We introduce additional structural supervision.\nThe two output channels are independent binary prediction tasks. We will not use softmax between them.\n\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"2048 × 2048 grayscale H-alpha image\"]\n    B[\"Overlapping tiles<br/>512 × 512\"]\n    C[\"ResNet34 Encoder<br/>(ImageNet initialized)\"]\n    D[\"U-Net Decoder\"]\n    E[\"Shared feature maps\"]\n    F[\"Two output channels\"]\n    \n    G[\"Filament mask<br/>probability\"]\n    H[\"Spine map<br/>probability\"]\n    \n    I[\"BCE + Dice\"]\n    J[\"Spine BCE + Dice\"]\n    \n    K[\"clDice\"]\n    L[\"Combined training objective\"]\n    M[\"Filament probability + spine probability\"]\n    N[\"Thresholding and instance separation\"]\n    O[\"Spine-guided watershed\"]\n    P[\"Individual filament masks\"]\n    Q[\"COCO RLE\"]\n\n    A --> B\n    B --> C\n    C --> D\n    D --> E\n    E --> F\n\n    F --> G\n    F --> H\n\n    G --> I\n    H --> J\n\n    I --> K\n    J --> K\n\n    K --> L\n    L --> M\n    M --> N\n    N --> O\n    O --> P\n    P --> Q\n```\n\nThe model predicts:\n\n$$\nP_{\\text{filament}}=\\sigma(z_0)\n$$\n\n$$\nP_{\\text{spine}}=\\sigma(z_1)\n$$\n\nThe two outputs are independent sigmoid probabilities.\n\nThe training objective:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\nL_{A1}=L_{\\text{mask}}+\\lambda_s L_{\\text{spine}}\n}\n$$\n\nWhere:\n\n$$\nL_{\\text{mask}}\n=\nL_{\\text{BCE}}\n+\nL_{\\text{Dice}}\n$$\n\n$$\nL_{\\text{spine}}\n=\nL_{\\text{Weighted BCE}}\n+\nL_{\\text{Dice}}\n$$","metadata":{},"attachments":{"e473e25e-71d3-4c05-ac35-243735c21223.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Optimizations\n\nA0 took approximately 10 minutes per epoch. We should not simply accept that as the cost of A1.\n\n**Optimization priorities**\n\n**1. Precompute annotation targets** - A0 rasterized polygons every time a photograph was loaded for training. A1 should precompute semantic and spine masks once per annotation batch and cache them as packed binary arrays.\n\nFor 1,154 batches, two packed 2048 × 2048 masks require approximately 1.21 GB uncompressed. This is much more manageable than retaining full uint8 masks for every batch.\n\n**2. Improve tile loading** - A0 returned [2, 25, 1, 512, 512], then flattened 50 tiles and ran seven separate micro-batches. A1 should use a tile-centric DataLoader with batches of 8–12 tiles. The selected annotation batch must be fixed per photograph for the entire epoch.\n\nUse two DataLoader workers initially, pinned memory and persistent workers. Benchmark eight versus twelve tiles before committing to twelve.\n\n**3. Reduce full-image validation frequency** - A0 ran complete 142-photo validation every epoch.\n\nA1 will perform full validation every three epochs. We will still save training checkpoints every epoch.\n\nThis avoids repeatedly spending inference time when the model has only made a small number of training updates.\n\n**4. Mixed precision and memory layout** - Retain CUDA FP16 AMP, GradScaler and gradient clipping. Benchmark channels-last memory layout after the initial smoke test.\n\nDo not introduce torch.compile initially; compilation overhead and compatibility issues could outweigh its benefits for this experiment.\n\n**5. Better learning-rate policy** - Use separate learning rates for pretrained and newly initialized parameters:\n- ResNet34 encoder: \\(1\\times10^{-4}\\)\n- U-Net decoder and output: \\(3\\times10^{-4}\\)\nThis allows the pretrained feature extractor to adapt more conservatively while the new output layer learns faster.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Artifact Protection","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1: EXPERIMENT ARTIFACT MANAGEMENT\n# ============================================================\n\nimport os\nimport json\nimport torch\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nRUN_ID = \"A1_SpineAux_ResNet34_Fold0_Seed2026\"\n\nRUN_ROOT = (\n    Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n    / \"solar_filament_experiments\"\n    / RUN_ID\n)\n\nCHECKPOINT_DIR = RUN_ROOT / \"checkpoints\"\nLOG_DIR = RUN_ROOT / \"logs\"\nPREDICTION_DIR = RUN_ROOT / \"predictions\"\nCACHE_DIR = RUN_ROOT / \"target_cache\"\nMANIFEST_DIR = RUN_ROOT / \"manifests\"\n\nfor directory in [\n    CHECKPOINT_DIR,\n    LOG_DIR,\n    PREDICTION_DIR,\n    CACHE_DIR,\n    MANIFEST_DIR\n]:\n    directory.mkdir(\n        parents=True,\n        exist_ok=True\n    )\n\n\ndef atomic_torch_save(obj, destination):\n\n    destination = Path(destination)\n\n    temp_path = destination.with_suffix(\n        destination.suffix + \".tmp\"\n    )\n\n    torch.save(obj, temp_path)\n\n    os.replace(temp_path, destination)\n\n\ndef atomic_json_save(obj, destination):\n\n    destination = Path(destination)\n\n    temp_path = destination.with_suffix(\n        destination.suffix + \".tmp\"\n    )\n\n    with open(temp_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(\n            obj,\n            f,\n            indent=4,\n            default=str\n        )\n\n    os.replace(temp_path, destination)\n\n\n# Copy frozen fold manifests.\nfor filename in [\n    \"folds_photo_level.csv\",\n    \"folds_batch_level.csv\",\n    \"folds_annotation_level.csv\"\n]:\n\n    source = WORK_DIR / filename\n\n    if not source.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(source)\n\n    import shutil\n\n    shutil.copy2(\n        source,\n        MANIFEST_DIR / filename\n    )\n\n\nA1_CONFIG = {\n\n    \"run_id\": RUN_ID,\n\n    \"seed\": 2026,\n\n    \"architecture\": \"SMP U-Net\",\n\n    \"encoder\": \"ResNet34\",\n\n    \"encoder_weights\": \"ImageNet\",\n\n    \"input_channels\": 1,\n\n    \"output_channels\": 2,\n\n    \"mask_channel\": 0,\n\n    \"spine_channel\": 1,\n\n    \"tile_size\": 512,\n\n    \"tile_stride\": 384,\n\n    \"spine_thickness\": 3,\n\n    \"training_folds\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n\n    \"validation_fold\": 0,\n\n    \"pytorch\": torch.__version__\n\n}\n\natomic_json_save(\n    A1_CONFIG,\n    RUN_ROOT / \"experiment_config.json\"\n)\n\nprint(\"A1 artifact system initialized.\")\nprint(RUN_ROOT)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Our checkpoint policy will be:\n- Save last.pt after every epoch, including the optimizer, scheduler, GradScaler and random states.\n- Save best.pt whenever validation improves.\n- Save training history and per-photo validation metrics.\n- Save configuration and normalization statistics.\n- Periodically preserve Kaggle Notebook Versions with output files enabled.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Spine Target Validity Audit","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# A1.3: SPINE ANNOTATION QUALITY AUDIT\n# ============================================================\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport cv2\n\nSPINE_THICKNESS = 3\nSPINE_AUDIT_SEED = 2026\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img for img in images_list\n}\n\nspine_records = []\nvalid_spine_indices = []\n\nfor idx, ann in enumerate(annotations_list):\n\n    info = image_info_by_id[ann[\"image_id\"]]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    spine = ann.get(\"spine\", [])\n\n    record = {\n        \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n        \"image_id\": ann[\"image_id\"],\n        \"file_name\": info[\"file_name\"],\n        \"valid\": False,\n        \"missing\": False,\n        \"out_of_bounds\": False,\n        \"spine_length_px\": np.nan,\n        \"n_points\": 0\n    }\n\n    if spine is None or len(spine) == 0:\n\n        record[\"missing\"] = True\n        spine_records.append(record)\n        continue\n\n    coords = np.asarray(\n        spine, dtype=np.float64\n    )\n\n    if (\n        coords.ndim != 1\n        or coords.size < 4\n        or coords.size % 2 != 0\n        or not np.isfinite(coords).all()\n    ):\n\n        spine_records.append(record)\n        continue\n\n    points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    out_of_bounds = np.any(\n        (points[:, 0] < 0)\n        | (points[:, 0] >= w)\n        | (points[:, 1] < 0)\n        | (points[:, 1] >= h)\n    )\n\n    length = np.linalg.norm(\n        np.diff(points, axis=0),\n        axis=1\n    ).sum()\n\n    record.update({\n\n        \"valid\": bool(length > 0),\n\n        \"out_of_bounds\": bool(out_of_bounds),\n\n        \"spine_length_px\": float(length),\n\n        \"n_points\": len(points)\n\n    })\n\n    if length > 0:\n        valid_spine_indices.append(idx)\n\n    spine_records.append(record)\n\n\nspine_audit_df = pd.DataFrame(spine_records)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"SPINE COORDINATE AUDIT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Total annotations:\", len(spine_audit_df))\n\nprint(\"Valid spines:\",\n      int(spine_audit_df[\"valid\"].sum()))\n\nprint(\"Missing spines:\",\n      int(spine_audit_df[\"missing\"].sum()))\n\nprint(\n    \"Out-of-bounds spines:\",\n    int(spine_audit_df[\"out_of_bounds\"].sum())\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSpine length distribution:\")\n\ndisplay(\n    spine_audit_df.loc[\n        spine_audit_df[\"valid\"],\n        \"spine_length_px\"\n    ].describe().round(2)\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Sampled geometric overlap audit\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(\n    SPINE_AUDIT_SEED\n)\n\nsample_indices = rng.choice(\n    valid_spine_indices,\n    size=min(128, len(valid_spine_indices)),\n    replace=False\n)\n\noverlap_records = []\n\nfor idx in sample_indices:\n\n    ann = annotations_list[int(idx)]\n\n    info = image_info_by_id[ann[\"image_id\"]]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    foreground = polygon_to_mask(\n        ann[\"segmentation\"], h, w\n    )\n\n    spine_mask = np.zeros(\n        (h, w),\n        dtype=np.uint8\n    )\n\n    points = np.rint(\n        np.asarray(\n            ann[\"spine\"], dtype=np.float64\n        ).reshape(-1, 2)\n    ).astype(np.int32).reshape(-1, 1, 2)\n\n    cv2.polylines(\n        spine_mask,\n        [points],\n        isClosed=False,\n        color=1,\n        thickness=SPINE_THICKNESS,\n        lineType=cv2.LINE_8\n    )\n\n    spine_pixels = int(spine_mask.sum())\n\n    inside_pixels = int(\n        np.logical_and(\n            spine_mask > 0,\n            foreground > 0\n        ).sum()\n    )\n\n    overlap_records.append({\n\n        \"ann_id\": ann[\"id\"],\n\n        \"spine_pixels\": spine_pixels,\n\n        \"inside_pixels\": inside_pixels,\n\n        \"inside_fraction\": (\n            inside_pixels / spine_pixels\n            if spine_pixels > 0 else np.nan\n        )\n\n    })\n\n\nspine_overlap_df = pd.DataFrame(\n    overlap_records\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- Sampled Spine/Filament Overlap ---\")\n\ndisplay(\n    spine_overlap_df[\"inside_fraction\"].describe().round(4)\n)\n\nspine_audit_df.to_csv(\n    CACHE_DIR / \"spine_coordinate_audit.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nspine_overlap_df.to_csv(\n    CACHE_DIR / \"spine_overlap_sample.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nSpine audit artifacts saved.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## TRAIN-FOLD NORMALIZATION STATISTICS Reused ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"assert normalization_stats[\"mean\"] == 0.3265100952768907 or np.isclose(\n    normalization_stats[\"mean\"],\n    0.3265100952769327\n)\n\nassert np.isclose(\n    normalization_stats[\"std\"],\n    0.22311718458989044\n)\n\nprint(\"Verified training-fold normalization is available.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Precompute and cache all annotation targets\n\nDuring A0, each Dataset access reconstructed polygon masks by calling polygon_to_mask().\n\nThat is unnecessary repeated CPU work.\n\nWe have 1,154 annotation batches. We will generate two masks for each:\n- Channel 0: semantic union of all filament polygons.\n- Channel 1: union of all three-pixel-wide spine bands.\n  \nWe will pack each mask into bits before storage.\n\n**Why bit packing?** A binary pixel only needs one bit rather than one byte.\n\nFor each annotation batch:\n- Two masks: 2 × 2048 × 2048 bits.\n- Packed storage: 1,048,576 bytes.\n- \nFor 1,154 batches, the complete cache occupies approximately 1.13 GiB.\n\nThe actual masks are reconstructed only when a Dataset sample needs them.\nThis is much better than storing roughly 9.7 GB of uncompressed uint8 masks","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# A1.4: PRECOMPUTE PACKED SEMANTIC + SPINE TARGETS\n# ============================================================\n\nimport os\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport cv2\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\n\nHEIGHT = 2048\nWIDTH = 2048\n\nSPINE_THICKNESS = 3\n\nBITORDER = \"little\"\n\nTARGET_CACHE_PATH = (\n    CACHE_DIR / \"packed_targets_v1.dat\"\n)\n\nTARGET_CACHE_META = (\n    CACHE_DIR / \"packed_targets_v1.json\"\n)\n\n# Stable annotation-batch ordering.\nbatch_ids_order = sorted(\n    img[\"id\"] for img in images_list\n)\n\nbatch_index = {\n    batch_id: idx\n    for idx, batch_id in enumerate(batch_ids_order)\n}\n\nimage_info_by_id = {\n    img[\"id\"]: img for img in images_list\n}\n\nassert len(batch_ids_order) == 1154\nassert len(batch_index) == 1154\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Define cache dimensions\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCACHE_SHAPE = (\n    len(batch_ids_order),\n    2,\n    HEIGHT,\n    WIDTH // 8\n)\n\nCACHE_DTYPE = np.uint8\n\nEXPECTED_CACHE_BYTES = (\n    np.prod(CACHE_SHAPE)\n    * np.dtype(CACHE_DTYPE).itemsize\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Expected cache size:\",\n    round(EXPECTED_CACHE_BYTES / 1024**3, 3),\n    \"GiB\"\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Create semantic and spine targets for one batch\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef create_semantic_spine_pair(batch_id):\n\n    info = image_info_by_id[batch_id]\n\n    h = int(info[\"height\"])\n    w = int(info[\"width\"])\n\n    if (h, w) != (HEIGHT, WIDTH):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Unexpected dimensions for {batch_id}\"\n        )\n\n    semantic_mask = np.zeros(\n        (h, w), dtype=np.uint8\n    )\n\n    spine_mask = np.zeros(\n        (h, w), dtype=np.uint8\n    )\n\n    annotations = image_id_to_anns.get(\n        batch_id, []\n    )\n\n    for ann in annotations:\n\n        # Ground-truth filament segmentation.\n        semantic_mask |= polygon_to_mask(\n            ann[\"segmentation\"],\n            h,\n            w\n        )\n\n        # Auxiliary spine supervision.\n        coords = np.asarray(\n            ann.get(\"spine\", []),\n            dtype=np.float64\n        )\n\n        if (\n            coords.ndim != 1\n            or coords.size < 4\n            or coords.size % 2 != 0\n            or not np.isfinite(coords).all()\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Invalid spine for annotation {ann['id']}\"\n            )\n\n        points = coords.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n        # No silent clipping: all coordinates passed\n        # our previous bounds audit.\n        if np.any(\n            (points[:, 0] < 0)\n            | (points[:, 0] >= w)\n            | (points[:, 1] < 0)\n            | (points[:, 1] >= h)\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Out-of-bounds spine: {ann['id']}\"\n            )\n\n        points = np.rint(\n            points\n        ).astype(np.int32).reshape(-1, 1, 2)\n\n        cv2.polylines(\n            spine_mask,\n            [points],\n            isClosed=False,\n            color=1,\n            thickness=SPINE_THICKNESS,\n            lineType=cv2.LINE_8\n        )\n\n    return semantic_mask, spine_mask\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Detect whether an existing cache is reusable\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ncache_valid = False\n\nif TARGET_CACHE_PATH.exists() and TARGET_CACHE_META.exists():\n\n    with open(TARGET_CACHE_META) as f:\n        saved_meta = json.load(f)\n\n    cache_valid = (\n\n        saved_meta.get(\"batch_ids\") == batch_ids_order\n\n        and saved_meta.get(\"shape\") == list(CACHE_SHAPE)\n\n        and saved_meta.get(\"spine_thickness\") == SPINE_THICKNESS\n\n        and TARGET_CACHE_PATH.stat().st_size\n        == EXPECTED_CACHE_BYTES\n\n    )\n\nif cache_valid:\n\n    print(\"Existing packed target cache is valid.\")\n    print(\"Skipping target reconstruction.\")\n\nelse:\n\n    print(\"Building fresh packed target cache...\")\n\n    temporary_path = TARGET_CACHE_PATH.with_suffix(\n        \".dat.tmp\"\n    )\n\n    if temporary_path.exists():\n        temporary_path.unlink()\n\n    cache_writer = np.memmap(\n        temporary_path,\n        dtype=CACHE_DTYPE,\n        mode=\"w+\",\n        shape=CACHE_SHAPE\n    )\n\n    for idx, batch_id in enumerate(\n        tqdm(batch_ids_order, desc=\"Rasterizing targets\")\n    ):\n\n        semantic_mask, spine_mask = (\n            create_semantic_spine_pair(batch_id)\n        )\n\n        # Shape: [2, 2048, 2048]\n        target_pair = np.stack(\n            [semantic_mask, spine_mask],\n            axis=0\n        )\n\n        # Pack 8 binary pixels into one uint8.\n        packed_target = np.packbits(\n            target_pair,\n            axis=-1,\n            bitorder=BITORDER\n        )\n\n        cache_writer[idx] = packed_target\n\n        del semantic_mask\n        del spine_mask\n        del target_pair\n        del packed_target\n\n        if (idx + 1) % 200 == 0:\n            cache_writer.flush()\n\n    cache_writer.flush()\n\n    del cache_writer\n\n    # Atomic finalization.\n    os.replace(\n        temporary_path,\n        TARGET_CACHE_PATH\n    )\n\n    metadata = {\n\n        \"version\": 1,\n\n        \"batch_ids\": batch_ids_order,\n\n        \"shape\": list(CACHE_SHAPE),\n\n        \"dtype\": \"uint8\",\n\n        \"bitorder\": BITORDER,\n\n        \"spine_thickness\": SPINE_THICKNESS,\n\n        \"height\": HEIGHT,\n\n        \"width\": WIDTH,\n\n        \"num_annotation_batches\": len(batch_ids_order)\n\n    }\n\n    atomic_json_save(\n        metadata,\n        TARGET_CACHE_META\n    )\n\n    print(\"Target cache successfully built.\")\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Open packed cache as read-only memory map\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntarget_cache = np.memmap(\n    TARGET_CACHE_PATH,\n    dtype=CACHE_DTYPE,\n    mode=\"r\",\n    shape=CACHE_SHAPE\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5. Utility to retrieve one batch's targets\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_batch_targets(batch_id):\n\n    idx = batch_index[batch_id]\n\n    packed = np.asarray(\n        target_cache[idx]\n    )\n\n    unpacked = np.unpackbits(\n        packed,\n        axis=-1,\n        count=WIDTH,\n        bitorder=BITORDER\n    )\n\n    return unpacked.astype(\n        np.uint8,\n        copy=False\n    )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6. Validate cache round-trip\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nsample_batch_id = batch_ids_order[100]\n\ndecoded = load_batch_targets(\n    sample_batch_id\n)\n\nassert decoded.shape == (\n    2, HEIGHT, WIDTH\n)\n\nassert set(np.unique(decoded)).issubset({0, 1})\n\nsemantic_sample = decoded[0]\nspine_sample = decoded[1]\n\nsemantic_pixels = int(\n    semantic_sample.sum()\n)\n\nspine_pixels = int(\n    spine_sample.sum()\n)\n\ninside_pixels = int(\n    np.logical_and(\n        semantic_sample > 0,\n        spine_sample > 0\n    ).sum()\n)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1 TARGET CACHE VALIDATION\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Sample batch:\", sample_batch_id)\n\nprint(\"Semantic foreground pixels:\", semantic_pixels)\n\nprint(\"Spine foreground pixels:\", spine_pixels)\n\nprint(\"Spine/semantic overlap pixels:\", inside_pixels)\n\nprint(\n    \"Spine inside fraction:\",\n    round(\n        inside_pixels / spine_pixels,\n        4\n    ) if spine_pixels else np.nan\n)\n\nprint(\"Decoded shape:\", decoded.shape)\n\nprint(\n    \"Cache disk size:\",\n    round(\n        TARGET_CACHE_PATH.stat().st_size / 1024**3,\n        3\n    ),\n    \"GiB\"\n)\n\n# Save index manifest for future reproducibility.\ncache_index_df = pd.DataFrame([\n\n    {\n        \"image_id\": batch_id,\n\n        \"file_name\": image_info_by_id[\n            batch_id\n        ][\"file_name\"],\n\n        \"cache_index\": idx,\n\n        \"fold\": int(\n            batch_df.set_index(\"image_id\")\n            .loc[batch_id, \"fold\"]\n        )\n\n    }\n\n    for idx, batch_id in enumerate(batch_ids_order)\n\n])\n\ncache_index_df.to_csv(\n    MANIFEST_DIR / \"target_cache_index.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nA1.4 TARGET CACHE: PASSED\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Calculate the auxiliary loss weight from actual data\n\nWe can measure the spine pixel prevalence using the training fold. We will calculate the prevalence using one average per physical photograph, so photographs with several annotation sets do not receive disproportionate statistical weight.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# A1.5: TRAINING-FOLD SPINE PREVALENCE\n# ============================================================\n\nbatch_ids_by_photo = (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"image_id\"]\n    .apply(list)\n    .to_dict()\n)\n\ntraining_photos = (\n    photo_df[\n        photo_df[\"fold\"].isin([1, 2, 3, 4])\n    ][\"file_name\"]\n    .tolist()\n)\n\nphoto_spine_prevalence = []\nphoto_mask_prevalence = []\n\nPIXELS_PER_PHOTO = HEIGHT * WIDTH\n\nfor file_name in tqdm(\n    training_photos,\n    desc=\"Measuring training target prevalence\"\n):\n\n    spine_fractions = []\n    mask_fractions = []\n\n    for batch_id in batch_ids_by_photo[file_name]:\n\n        idx = batch_index[batch_id]\n\n        packed = target_cache[idx]\n\n        # Count positive bits without constructing\n        # a complete mask array.\n        spine_positive = np.unpackbits(\n            packed[1],\n            axis=-1,\n            bitorder=BITORDER\n        ).sum()\n\n        mask_positive = np.unpackbits(\n            packed[0],\n            axis=-1,\n            bitorder=BITORDER\n        ).sum()\n\n        spine_fractions.append(\n            spine_positive / PIXELS_PER_PHOTO\n        )\n\n        mask_fractions.append(\n            mask_positive / PIXELS_PER_PHOTO\n        )\n\n    # Average annotation sets within each physical photo.\n    photo_spine_prevalence.append(\n        np.mean(spine_fractions)\n    )\n\n    photo_mask_prevalence.append(\n        np.mean(mask_fractions)\n    )\n\nmean_spine_prevalence = float(\n    np.mean(photo_spine_prevalence)\n)\n\nmean_mask_prevalence = float(\n    np.mean(photo_mask_prevalence)\n)\n\nraw_pos_weight = (\n    (1.0 - mean_spine_prevalence)\n    / mean_spine_prevalence\n)\n\n# Square-root balancing is a conservative initial policy.\n# Dice loss will also contribute directly to foreground overlap.\nspine_pos_weight = float(\n    np.clip(\n        np.sqrt(raw_pos_weight),\n        1.0,\n        20.0\n    )\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nTraining foreground prevalence:\")\nprint(\"Filament:\", mean_mask_prevalence)\nprint(\"Spine:\", mean_spine_prevalence)\n\nprint(\"\\nSpine raw negative/positive ratio:\", raw_pos_weight)\n\nprint(\"Selected spine BCE positive weight:\", spine_pos_weight)\n\ntarget_statistics = {\n\n    \"mean_mask_prevalence\": mean_mask_prevalence,\n\n    \"mean_spine_prevalence\": mean_spine_prevalence,\n\n    \"raw_spine_negative_positive_ratio\": float(raw_pos_weight),\n\n    \"spine_pos_weight\": spine_pos_weight,\n\n    \"lambda_spine\": 0.2\n\n}\n\natomic_json_save(\n    target_statistics,\n    RUN_ROOT / \"target_statistics.json\"\n)\n\nprint(\"\\nTarget statistics saved.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"The square-root weighting is a conservative starting heuristic. It prevents an extreme negative-to-positive ratio from completely dominating the auxiliary BCE loss.\n\nWe will examine the resulting value before finalizing the loss","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## PHOTO-CENTRIC DATASET\n\nWe need to connect the three pieces: one physical image, one annotation set selected for that training epoch, and its cached semantic + spine masks. \n\nOne dataset item represents one physical photograph, not one tile. It loads the JPEG once, selects one of that photo's annotation batches, decodes the cached target pair, and produces all 25 tiles. This preserves the sampling policy we used for A0 and avoids reading the same photograph 25 times.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### verify the inputs and prepare the partitions","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1.6: A1 PHOTO-CENTRIC DATA PIPELINE\n# ============================================================\n\nimport cv2\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Verify all upstream dependencies\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nassert TRAIN_IMG_DIR.is_dir(), (\n    f\"Training image directory not found: {TRAIN_IMG_DIR}\"\n)\n\nassert len(photo_df) == 707\nassert len(batch_df) == 1154\nassert df_eda[\"ann_id\"].nunique() == 8199\n\nassert target_cache.shape == CACHE_SHAPE\nassert target_cache.dtype == np.uint8\n\nassert len(batch_index) == 1154\n\nassert normalization_stats[\"std\"] > 0\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. Establish train and validation photographs\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntrain_photo_df = (\n    photo_df[\n        photo_df[\"fold\"].isin([1, 2, 3, 4])\n    ]\n    .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nval_photo_df = (\n    photo_df[\n        photo_df[\"fold\"] == 0\n    ]\n    .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nassert len(train_photo_df) == 565\nassert len(val_photo_df) == 142\n\nassert set(train_photo_df[\"file_name\"]).isdisjoint(\n    set(val_photo_df[\"file_name\"])\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3. Map each physical photograph to its annotation batches\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbatch_ids_by_photo = (\n    batch_df.groupby(\"file_name\")[\"image_id\"]\n    .apply(lambda ids: sorted(ids.tolist()))\n    .to_dict()\n)\n\nassert len(batch_ids_by_photo) == 707\n\nassert set(batch_ids_by_photo) == set(\n    photo_df[\"file_name\"]\n)\n\nassert sum(\n    len(ids) for ids in batch_ids_by_photo.values()\n) == 1154\n\n# Ensure every batch ID has a cache position.\nfor batch_ids in batch_ids_by_photo.values():\n    for batch_id in batch_ids:\n        assert batch_id in batch_index\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4. Check one physical image file\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nsample_filename = train_photo_df.iloc[0][\"file_name\"]\n\nsample_image_path = TRAIN_IMG_DIR / sample_filename\n\nassert sample_image_path.is_file()\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1 DATA PIPELINE INPUT VALIDATION\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Training image directory:\", TRAIN_IMG_DIR)\nprint(\"Training physical photos:\", len(train_photo_df))\nprint(\"Validation physical photos:\", len(val_photo_df))\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", len(batch_index))\nprint(\"Packed cache shape:\", target_cache.shape)\nprint(\"Sample image:\", sample_filename)\n\nprint(\"\\nA1 INPUT VALIDATION: PASSED\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Training dataset\n\nOne item represents one physical photograph.\n\nIt selects one annotation set deterministically for the current epoch, loads the physical image once, retrieves the cached semantic and spine targets, and extracts all 25 tiles. \n\nThe dataset returns raw uint8 image and target tensors. It does not normalize or augment the data. We will apply the same normalization policy as A0 in the training loop, but with both target channels transformed together.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1 TRAINING DATASET\n# ============================================================\n\nclass A1PhotoTileDataset(Dataset):\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        photo_records,\n        image_dir,\n        batch_ids_by_photo,\n        target_cache,\n        batch_index,\n        tile_size=512,\n        stride=384,\n        seed=2026\n    ):\n\n        self.photos = (\n            photo_records\n            .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n            .reset_index(drop=True)\n        )\n\n        self.image_dir = Path(image_dir)\n\n        self.batch_ids_by_photo = batch_ids_by_photo\n\n        self.target_cache = target_cache\n        self.batch_index = batch_index\n\n        self.tile_size = tile_size\n        self.stride = stride\n\n        self.seed = seed\n        self.epoch = 0\n\n        self.height = 2048\n        self.width = 2048\n\n        self.bitorder = BITORDER\n\n        # Verify every photograph has annotation options.\n        for filename in self.photos[\"file_name\"]:\n\n            if filename not in self.batch_ids_by_photo:\n\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"No annotation batch found: {filename}\"\n                )\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.photos)\n\n    def set_epoch(self, epoch):\n        self.epoch = int(epoch)\n\n    def select_annotation_batch(self, index):\n\n        photo = self.photos.iloc[index]\n\n        filename = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\n        available_batches = self.batch_ids_by_photo[\n            filename\n        ]\n\n        # Reproducible selection by seed, epoch and photo index.\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(\n            np.random.SeedSequence([\n                self.seed,\n                self.epoch,\n                int(index)\n            ])\n        )\n\n        selected_position = int(\n            rng.integers(0, len(available_batches))\n        )\n\n        return available_batches[selected_position]\n\n    def __getitem__(self, index):\n\n        photo = self.photos.iloc[index]\n\n        filename = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 1. Select one annotation set for this photo and epoch\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        selected_batch = self.select_annotation_batch(index)\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 2. Load the physical grayscale image once\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        image_path = self.image_dir / filename\n\n        image = cv2.imread(\n            str(image_path),\n            cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n        )\n\n        if image is None:\n\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Failed to read image: {image_path}\"\n            )\n\n        if image.shape != (self.height, self.width):\n\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Unexpected image dimensions: {filename}\"\n            )\n\n        if image.dtype != np.uint8:\n\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"Unexpected image dtype: {filename}\"\n            )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 3. Decode the cached semantic + spine targets\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        cache_position = self.batch_index[selected_batch]\n\n        packed_targets = np.asarray(\n            self.target_cache[cache_position]\n        )\n\n        targets = np.unpackbits(\n            packed_targets,\n            axis=-1,\n            count=self.width,\n            bitorder=self.bitorder\n        )\n\n        # Shape: [2, 2048, 2048]\n        # Channel 0 = semantic filament mask\n        # Channel 1 = auxiliary spine mask\n\n        targets = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            targets,\n            dtype=np.uint8\n        )\n\n        semantic_mask = targets[0]\n        spine_mask = targets[1]\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 4. Extract all 25 tiles using the existing utility\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        tiles = extract_tiles(\n            image,\n            semantic_mask,\n            spine_mask=spine_mask,\n            tile_size=self.tile_size,\n            stride=self.stride,\n            min_filament_pixels=0\n        )\n\n        if len(tiles) != 25:\n\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Expected 25 tiles, got {len(tiles)}\"\n            )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 5. Organize image and target tiles\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        # [25, 1, 512, 512]\n        image_tiles = np.stack([\n            tile[\"img_tile\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ])[:, None, :, :]\n\n        # [25, 2, 512, 512]\n        target_tiles = np.stack([\n            np.stack(\n                [\n                    tile[\"mask_tile\"],\n                    tile[\"spine_tile\"]\n                ],\n                axis=0\n            )\n            for tile in tiles\n        ])\n\n        # Pixel counts for diagnostics.\n        semantic_pixel_counts = np.asarray([\n            tile[\"pixel_count\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ], dtype=np.int64)\n\n        spine_pixel_counts = np.asarray([\n            int(tile[\"spine_tile\"].sum())\n            for tile in tiles\n        ], dtype=np.int64)\n\n        tile_coords = np.asarray([\n            tile[\"coords\"]\n            for tile in tiles\n        ], dtype=np.int32)\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 6. Return raw uint8 tensors\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        return {\n\n            \"images\": torch.from_numpy(\n                np.ascontiguousarray(image_tiles)\n            ),\n\n            \"targets\": torch.from_numpy(\n                np.ascontiguousarray(target_tiles)\n            ),\n\n            \"semantic_pixel_counts\": torch.from_numpy(\n                semantic_pixel_counts\n            ),\n\n            \"spine_pixel_counts\": torch.from_numpy(\n                spine_pixel_counts\n            ),\n\n            \"tile_coords\": torch.from_numpy(\n                tile_coords\n            ),\n\n            \"file_name\": filename,\n\n            \"batch_id\": selected_batch,\n\n            \"fold\": int(photo[\"fold\"])\n        }","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Validation dataset\n\nFor validation, we must not randomly select one annotation batch.\n\nWe predict each physical photograph once and compare the resulting semantic prediction against every available annotation batch for that photograph.\n\nThe validation dataset therefore uses the cached semantic masks for every annotator.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1 VALIDATION DATASET\n# ============================================================\n\nclass A1ValidationPhotoDataset(Dataset):\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        photo_records,\n        image_dir,\n        batch_ids_by_photo,\n        target_cache,\n        batch_index\n    ):\n\n        self.photos = (\n            photo_records\n            .sort_values(\"file_name\")\n            .reset_index(drop=True)\n        )\n\n        self.image_dir = Path(image_dir)\n\n        self.batch_ids_by_photo = batch_ids_by_photo\n\n        self.target_cache = target_cache\n        self.batch_index = batch_index\n\n        self.height = 2048\n        self.width = 2048\n\n        self.bitorder = BITORDER\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.photos)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, index):\n\n        photo = self.photos.iloc[index]\n\n        filename = photo[\"file_name\"]\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 1. Load the physical image\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        image_path = self.image_dir / filename\n\n        image = cv2.imread(\n            str(image_path),\n            cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE\n        )\n\n        if image is None:\n\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f\"Failed to read image: {image_path}\"\n            )\n\n        if image.shape != (self.height, self.width):\n\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"Unexpected dimensions: {filename}\"\n            )\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n        # 2. Retrieve every annotation batch for this photo\n        # ----------------------------------------------------\n\n        annotation_batches = self.batch_ids_by_photo[\n            filename\n        ]\n\n        semantic_masks = []\n\n        for batch_id in annotation_batches:\n\n            cache_position = self.batch_index[batch_id]\n\n            # Decode only channel 0.\n            # The primary validation metric is semantic overlap.\n\n            packed_semantic = np.asarray(\n                self.target_cache[\n                    cache_position,\n                    0\n                ]\n            )\n\n            semantic_mask = np.unpackbits(\n                packed_semantic,\n                axis=-1,\n                count=self.width,\n                bitorder=self.bitorder\n            )\n\n            semantic_masks.append(\n                semantic_mask.astype(\n                    np.uint8,\n                    copy=False\n                )\n            )\n\n        # [N_annotation_sets, 1, 2048, 2048]\n        target_masks = np.stack(\n            semantic_masks,\n            axis=0\n        )[:, None, :, :]\n\n        image = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            image[None, :, :]\n        )\n\n        target_masks = np.ascontiguousarray(\n            target_masks\n        )\n\n        return {\n\n            \"image\": torch.from_numpy(image),\n\n            \"target_masks\": torch.from_numpy(\n                target_masks\n            ),\n\n            \"file_name\": filename,\n\n            \"batch_ids\": annotation_batches,\n\n            \"fold\": int(photo[\"fold\"])\n        }\n\n\nprint(\"A1 dataset classes defined.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Construct the DataLoaders\n\nWe retain the A0 sampling structure:\n- Two physical photographs per training batch.\n- All 25 tiles per photograph.\n- Eight tiles per GPU microbatch later in the training loop.\n- One physical photograph per validation batch.\n- No multiprocessing workers initially.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1.7: DATALOADER CONSTRUCTION\n# ============================================================\n\nA1_SEED = 2026\n\ntorch.manual_seed(A1_SEED)\nnp.random.seed(A1_SEED)\n\na1_train_dataset = A1PhotoTileDataset(\n    photo_records=train_photo_df,\n    image_dir=TRAIN_IMG_DIR,\n    batch_ids_by_photo=batch_ids_by_photo,\n    target_cache=target_cache,\n    batch_index=batch_index,\n    tile_size=512,\n    stride=384,\n    seed=A1_SEED\n)\n\na1_val_dataset = A1ValidationPhotoDataset(\n    photo_records=val_photo_df,\n    image_dir=TRAIN_IMG_DIR,\n    batch_ids_by_photo=batch_ids_by_photo,\n    target_cache=target_cache,\n    batch_index=batch_index\n)\n\n\n# Separate generator for reproducible DataLoader shuffling.\na1_loader_generator = torch.Generator()\n\na1_loader_generator.manual_seed(A1_SEED)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Training loader\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\na1_train_loader = DataLoader(\n    a1_train_dataset,\n    batch_size=2,\n    shuffle=True,\n    num_workers=0,\n    pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available(),\n    drop_last=False,\n    generator=a1_loader_generator\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Validation loader\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\na1_val_loader = DataLoader(\n    a1_val_dataset,\n    batch_size=1,\n    shuffle=False,\n    num_workers=0,\n    pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available()\n)\n\n\nprint(\"A1 training photos:\", len(a1_train_dataset))\nprint(\"A1 validation photos:\", len(a1_val_dataset))\n\nprint(\"Training batches per epoch:\", len(a1_train_loader))\nprint(\"Validation batches:\", len(a1_val_loader))","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Data Loader Smoke test","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1.8: A1 DATASET AND DATALOADER SMOKE TEST\n# ============================================================\n\na1_train_dataset.set_epoch(0)\n\ntrain_batch = next(iter(a1_train_loader))\n\nx = train_batch[\"images\"]\ny = train_batch[\"targets\"]\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1 TRAINING DATALOADER\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Image shape:\", tuple(x.shape))\nprint(\"Target shape:\", tuple(y.shape))\n\nprint(\"Image dtype:\", x.dtype)\nprint(\"Target dtype:\", y.dtype)\n\nprint(\"Selected photographs:\", train_batch[\"file_name\"])\nprint(\"Selected annotation batches:\", train_batch[\"batch_id\"])\n\nprint(\n    \"Positive semantic tiles:\",\n    (train_batch[\"semantic_pixel_counts\"] > 0).sum(dim=1)\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Positive spine tiles:\",\n    (train_batch[\"spine_pixel_counts\"] > 0).sum(dim=1)\n)\n\nassert x.shape == (2, 25, 1, 512, 512)\nassert y.shape == (2, 25, 2, 512, 512)\n\nassert x.dtype == torch.uint8\nassert y.dtype == torch.uint8\n\nassert y.min() >= 0\nassert y.max() <= 1\n\nassert train_batch[\"tile_coords\"].shape == (2, 25, 4)\n\n# Ensure every selected annotation batch belongs to its photo.\nfor filename, batch_id in zip(\n    train_batch[\"file_name\"],\n    train_batch[\"batch_id\"]\n):\n\n    assert batch_id in batch_ids_by_photo[filename]\n\n# Check that stored counts agree with the target tensors.\nsemantic_counts_check = y[:, :, 0].sum(\n    dim=(-2, -1)\n)\n\nspine_counts_check = y[:, :, 1].sum(\n    dim=(-2, -1)\n)\n\nassert torch.equal(\n    semantic_counts_check,\n    train_batch[\"semantic_pixel_counts\"]\n)\n\nassert torch.equal(\n    spine_counts_check,\n    train_batch[\"spine_pixel_counts\"]\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Epoch-wise annotation selection check\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\na1_train_dataset.set_epoch(0)\n\nselection_epoch_0_a = (\n    a1_train_dataset.select_annotation_batch(0)\n)\n\nselection_epoch_0_b = (\n    a1_train_dataset.select_annotation_batch(0)\n)\n\nassert selection_epoch_0_a == selection_epoch_0_b\n\na1_train_dataset.set_epoch(1)\n\nselection_epoch_1 = (\n    a1_train_dataset.select_annotation_batch(0)\n)\n\nassert selection_epoch_1 in batch_ids_by_photo[\n    a1_train_dataset.photos.iloc[0][\"file_name\"]\n]\n\nprint(\"\\nAnnotation selection:\")\nprint(\"Epoch 0:\", selection_epoch_0_a)\nprint(\"Epoch 1:\", selection_epoch_1)\n\nprint(\n    \"Selection is deterministic for a given photo and epoch.\"\n)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Validation loader check\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nval_batch = next(iter(a1_val_loader))\n\nval_image = val_batch[\"image\"]\nval_targets = val_batch[\"target_masks\"]\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1 VALIDATION DATALOADER\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Image shape:\", tuple(val_image.shape))\nprint(\"All annotation targets:\", tuple(val_targets.shape))\n\nprint(\"Filename:\", val_batch[\"file_name\"])\nprint(\"Annotation batches:\", val_batch[\"batch_ids\"])\n\nassert val_image.shape == (1, 1, 2048, 2048)\n\nassert val_targets.ndim == 5\nassert val_targets.shape[0] == 1\nassert val_targets.shape[2:] == (1, 2048, 2048)\n\nassert val_targets.shape[1] == len(\n    val_batch[\"batch_ids\"]\n)\n\nassert val_image.dtype == torch.uint8\nassert val_targets.dtype == torch.uint8\n\nassert val_targets.min() >= 0\nassert val_targets.max() <= 1\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# Final checks\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1 COMPUTE ENVIRONMENT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"PyTorch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"CUDA available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\n\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n\n    print(\"GPU:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n\n    print(\n        \"GPU memory:\",\n        round(\n            torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory\n            / 1024**3,\n            2\n        ),\n        \"GB\"\n    )\n\n\nprint(\"\\nA1.8 DATASET AND DATALOADER: PASSED\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Lock A1 config","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1 BASE CONFIGURATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport random\n\nA1_SEED = 2026\n\nA1_LAMBDA_SPINE = 0.2\nA1_SPINE_POS_WEIGHT = float(spine_pos_weight)\n\nA1_LEARNING_RATE = 3e-4\nA1_WEIGHT_DECAY = 1e-4\n\nA1_GRADIENT_CLIP = 1.0\n\nA1_PHOTO_BATCH_SIZE = 2\nA1_MICRO_BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\nassert \"A1_CONFIG\" in globals()\nassert \"target_statistics\" in globals()\n\nassert np.isclose(\n    A1_SPINE_POS_WEIGHT,\n    target_statistics[\"spine_pos_weight\"]\n)\n\nA1_CONFIG.update({\n\n    \"seed\": A1_SEED,\n\n    \"lambda_spine\": A1_LAMBDA_SPINE,\n\n    \"spine_pos_weight\": A1_SPINE_POS_WEIGHT,\n\n    \"learning_rate\": A1_LEARNING_RATE,\n\n    \"weight_decay\": A1_WEIGHT_DECAY,\n\n    \"gradient_clip\": A1_GRADIENT_CLIP,\n\n    \"photo_batch_size\": A1_PHOTO_BATCH_SIZE,\n\n    \"tile_micro_batch\": A1_MICRO_BATCH_SIZE,\n\n    \"amp\": True,\n\n    \"amp_dtype\": \"float16\"\n\n})\n\nrandom.seed(A1_SEED)\nnp.random.seed(A1_SEED)\n\ntorch.manual_seed(A1_SEED)\ntorch.cuda.manual_seed_all(A1_SEED)\n\natomic_json_save(\n    A1_CONFIG,\n    RUN_ROOT / \"experiment_config.json\"\n)\n\nprint(\"A1 base configuration locked.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## A1-Model Kathamo Pujo\n\nWe retain the architecture and encoder from A0, changing only the output head from one channel to two. \n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[\"2048×2048 Image<br/>→ 512×512 Tiles\"]\n    B[\"ResNet34 Encoder\"]\n    C[\"U-Net Decoder\"]\n    D[\"Filament Mask\"]\n    E[\"Spine Mask\"]\n\n    A --> B --> C\n    C --> D\n    C --> E\n```\n\n*Both outputs are independent logits. We apply sigmoid separately during loss calculation and inference, not softmax.*\n\n**Why are we not using softmax ?**\n\nThe two outputs are not mutually exclusive classes. A pixel can belong to a filament and also lie along its spine. The spine is a subset-like auxiliary target within the filament, so independent sigmoid outputs are appropriate.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1.9: TWO-OUTPUT U-NET CONSTRUCTION\n# ============================================================\n\na1_model = smp.Unet(\n    encoder_name=\"resnet34\",\n    encoder_weights=\"imagenet\",\n    in_channels=1,\n    classes=2,\n    activation=None\n).to(device)\n\na1_total_params = sum(\n    p.numel() for p in a1_model.parameters()\n)\n\na1_trainable_params = sum(\n    p.numel()\n    for p in a1_model.parameters()\n    if p.requires_grad\n)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"A1: SPINE-ASSISTED MULTI-TASK U-NET\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nprint(\"Architecture: U-Net\")\nprint(\"Encoder: ResNet34\")\nprint(\"Encoder initialization: ImageNet\")\n\nprint(\n    \"Input channels:\",\n    a1_model.encoder.conv1.in_channels\n)\n\nprint(\n    \"Output channels:\",\n    a1_model.segmentation_head[0].out_channels\n)\n\nprint(\"Total parameters:\", f\"{a1_total_params:,}\")\nprint(\"Trainable parameters:\", f\"{a1_trainable_params:,}\")\n\nprint(\n    \"FP32 parameter memory:\",\n    f\"{a1_total_params * 4 / 1024**2:.2f} MB\"\n)\n\nassert a1_model.encoder.conv1.in_channels == 1\nassert a1_model.segmentation_head[0].out_channels == 2\n\nassert a1_model.training is True\n\nprint(\"\\nA1 model constructed successfully.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Dice loss\n\nFor A0:\n$$\nL_{A0}=L_{\\text{BCE,mask}}+L_{\\text{Dice,mask}}\n$$\n\nFor A1:\n$$\n\\boxed{\nL_{A1}=L_{\\text{mask}}+0.2L_{\\text{spine}}\n}\n$$\n\nwhere:\n$$\nL_{\\text{mask}}=L_{\\text{BCE,mask}}+L_{\\text{Dice,mask}}\n$$\n\n$$\nL_{\\text{spine}}=L_{\\text{weighted BCE,spine}}+L_{\\text{Dice,spine}}\n$$\n\nThe mask and spine losses are calculated separately. This is important because the semantic mask and the spine have different foreground prevalence.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# A1.10: MULTI-TASK LOSS IMPLEMENTATION\n# ============================================================\n\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n\ndef a1_soft_dice_loss(logits, targets, smooth=1.0):\n\n    \"\"\"\n    logits:\n        [B, 1, H, W]\n\n    targets:\n        [B, 1, H, W]\n\n    Dice is calculated separately per tile, then averaged.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    logits = logits.float()\n    targets = targets.float()\n\n    probabilities = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n\n    intersection = (\n        probabilities * targets\n    ).sum(dim=(2, 3))\n\n    denominator = (\n        probabilities.sum(dim=(2, 3))\n        + targets.sum(dim=(2, 3))\n    )\n\n    dice = (\n        2.0 * intersection + smooth\n    ) / (\n        denominator + smooth\n    )\n\n    return 1.0 - dice.mean()","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def a1_loss_function(\n    logits,\n    targets,\n    spine_pos_weight,\n    lambda_spine=0.2\n):\n\n    \"\"\"\n    logits:\n        [B, 2, H, W]\n\n    targets:\n        [B, 2, H, W]\n\n    Channel 0 = semantic filament\n    Channel 1 = auxiliary spine\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if logits.shape != targets.shape:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Logit/target mismatch: \"\n            f\"{logits.shape} vs {targets.shape}\"\n        )\n\n    # Explicit FP32 loss calculations.\n    logits = logits.float()\n    targets = targets.float()\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n    # Channel 0: semantic filament segmentation\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n\n    mask_logits = logits[:, 0:1]\n    mask_targets = targets[:, 0:1]\n\n    mask_bce = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(\n        mask_logits,\n        mask_targets\n    )\n\n    mask_dice = a1_soft_dice_loss(\n        mask_logits,\n        mask_targets\n    )\n\n    mask_loss = mask_bce + mask_dice\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n    # Channel 1: auxiliary spine segmentation\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n\n    spine_logits = logits[:, 1:2]\n    spine_targets = targets[:, 1:2]\n\n    pos_weight_tensor = torch.tensor(\n        [spine_pos_weight],\n        device=logits.device,\n        dtype=torch.float32\n    )\n\n    spine_bce = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(\n        spine_logits,\n        spine_targets,\n        pos_weight=pos_weight_tensor\n    )\n\n    spine_dice = a1_soft_dice_loss(\n        spine_logits,\n        spine_targets\n    )\n\n    spine_loss = spine_bce + spine_dice\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n    # Final multi-task objective\n    # --------------------------------------------------------\n\n    total_loss = (\n        mask_loss\n        + lambda_spine * spine_loss\n    )\n\n    return {\n\n        \"total\": total_loss,\n\n        \"mask_loss\": mask_loss,\n\n        \"mask_bce\": mask_bce,\n\n        \"mask_dice\": mask_dice,\n\n        \"spine_loss\": spine_loss,\n\n        \"spine_bce\": spine_bce,\n\n        \"spine_dice\": spine_dice\n\n    }\n\n\nprint(\"A1 multi-task loss functions defined.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Verify the model, losses and gradient flow\n\nBefore testing the model, let's verify that multi-annotator sampling actually has alternatives for a photograph with multiple annotation batches. This confirms that the training pipeline can expose the model to alternative annotator masks over different epochs. It does not require every epoch to select a different annotation set.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# MULTI-ANNOTATOR EPOCH SAMPLING CHECK\n# =======================================================